// English content. Ids are language-independent keys: keep them identical in every language.
// E: profiles. t: type (casa, figura, criatura, magia, lugar, mundo). g: group in the list. c: color key. n: name. s: subtitle.
// p: paragraphs. f: fact sheet as [label, value]. br/bt: breakdown list and its optional heading.
// x: what comes from outside the seven books, as [source, text] (source keys: lt, site, ent, peca, af).
// In the texts, [[id|label]] becomes a link to another profile.
const E = {
/* ---------- HOUSES ---------- */
grifinoria:{t:"casa",g:"Hogwarts house",c:"grif",n:"Gryffindor",s:"The house of courage",
 p:[`Founded by [[godrico|Godric Gryffindor]], it gathers the students in whom the [[chapeu|Sorting Hat]] sees courage, daring and chivalry. Its crest shows a golden lion on a scarlet field.`,
 `The common room is in a tower, entered on the seventh floor through the portrait of the Fat Lady, who opens only for the current password. It is the house of [[harry|Harry]], [[rony|Ron]] and [[hermione|Hermione]], of [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]], [[mcgonagall|McGonagall]] and [[hagrid|Hagrid]], of the [[marotos|Marauders]] and of the whole [[weasley|Weasley family]].`,
 `The rivalry with [[sonserina|Slytherin]] comes from the quarrel between the two founders and runs through every book, from the House Cup to [[quadribol|Quidditch]].`],
 f:[["Crest","On a scarlet field, a golden lion rampant"],["Founder","Godric Gryffindor"],["Colours","Scarlet and gold"],["Animal","Lion"],["Element","Fire"],["Hourglass gems","Rubies"],["Ghost","Nearly Headless Nick (Sir Nicholas de Mimsy-Porpington), beheaded on 31 October 1492"],["Head of House","Minerva McGonagall"],["Relic","The Sword of Gryffindor"]],
 x:[["ent","The author linked the four elements to the houses in a 2005 interview: fire, water, air and earth."],["site","Minerva McGonagall and Peter Pettigrew were 'Hatstalls': the Sorting Hat took more than five minutes to decide. She was torn between Gryffindor and Ravenclaw, he between Gryffindor and Slytherin."]]},
sonserina:{t:"casa",g:"Hogwarts house",c:"sons",n:"Slytherin",s:"The house of ambition",
 p:[`Founded by [[salazar|Salazar Slytherin]], it prizes ambition, cunning, leadership and resourcefulness. The founder wanted to admit only students from wizarding families, and for centuries the house carried a reputation for favouring [[sangue|pure-bloods]]. Its crest shows a silver serpent on a green field.`,
 `The common room is in the dungeons, behind a smooth stretch of stone wall that opens with a password. Part of it extends under the lake, and the light inside is greenish.`,
 `[[voldemort|Voldemort]] and most of the [[comensais|Death Eaters]] came from it, but so did [[snape|Snape]], [[slughorn|Slughorn]] and [[regulo|Regulus Black]], who died or fought against him. In the Battle of Hogwarts the house's students were evacuated from the castle, and Slughorn returned bringing reinforcements.`],
 f:[["Crest","On a green field, a silver serpent"],["Founder","Salazar Slytherin"],["Colours","Green and silver"],["Animal","Serpent"],["Element","Water"],["Hourglass gems","Emeralds"],["Ghost","The Bloody Baron"],["Head of House","Severus Snape until 1997, then Horace Slughorn"],["Relic","Slytherin's locket"]],
 x:[["site","Merlin was a Slytherin, according to the author's writings."],["peca","In 2017, Albus Severus Potter is sorted into Slytherin and befriends Scorpius Malfoy."]]},
corvinal:{t:"casa",g:"Hogwarts house",c:"corv",n:"Ravenclaw",s:"The house of wit",
 p:[`Founded by [[rowena|Rowena Ravenclaw]], it looks for intelligence, a thirst for knowledge, creativity and originality. The crest in the books shows a bronze eagle on a blue field. The films swapped it for a raven and for blue and silver.`,
 `The common room is in a tower on the west side of the castle. There is no password: a bronze eagle-shaped knocker asks a question, and whoever answers well gets in. Whoever gets it wrong waits for the next person.`,
 `[[luna|Luna Lovegood]], Cho Chang, Professor Flitwick and [[lockhart|Gilderoy Lockhart]] belong to Ravenclaw. The house ghost, the Grey Lady, is Helena Ravenclaw, the founder's daughter, and she was the one who stole her mother's [[horcruxes|diadem]].`],
 f:[["Crest","On a blue field, a bronze eagle in the books and a raven in the films"],["Founder","Rowena Ravenclaw"],["Colours","Blue and bronze"],["Animal","Eagle"],["Element","Air"],["Hourglass gems","Sapphires"],["Ghost","The Grey Lady (Helena Ravenclaw)"],["Head of House","Filius Flitwick"],["Relic","Ravenclaw's diadem"]],
 x:[["site","The author's writings place in Ravenclaw the wandmaker Ollivander, Professor Trelawney, Professor Quirrell and Moaning Myrtle."]]},
lufalufa:{t:"casa",g:"Hogwarts house",c:"lufa",n:"Hufflepuff",s:"The house of loyalty",
 p:[`Founded by [[helga|Helga Hufflepuff]], it prizes hard work, patience, loyalty and fair play. While the other founders chose a certain kind of student, Helga accepted everyone and treated them all the same. Its crest shows a black badger on a yellow field.`,
 `The common room is in the basement, along the same corridor as the kitchens. It is round, low-ceilinged, full of plants and light.`,
 `[[cedrico|Cedric Diggory]], [[tonks|Nymphadora Tonks]], [[newt|Newt Scamander]] and Professor Sprout belong to Hufflepuff. In the Battle of Hogwarts it was the house that stayed to fight in the greatest numbers after Gryffindor.`],
 f:[["Crest","On a yellow field, a badger"],["Founder","Helga Hufflepuff"],["Colours","Yellow and black"],["Animal","Badger"],["Element","Earth"],["Hourglass gems","Yellow diamonds"],["Ghost","The Fat Friar"],["Head of House","Pomona Sprout"],["Relic","Hufflepuff's cup"]],
 x:[["site","The entrance is behind a stack of barrels. You have to tap the rhythm of 'Helga Hufflepuff' on the second barrel from the bottom in the middle row. Whoever taps the wrong barrel or the wrong rhythm gets drenched in vinegar."],["site","In more than a thousand years, the Hufflepuff common room has never been seen by anyone from another house. It is the only one of the four."],["ent","Teddy Lupin, the son of Lupin and Tonks, was a Hufflepuff, like his mother."]]},

/* ---------- FOUNDERS ---------- */
godrico:{t:"figura",g:"The founders",c:"grif",n:"Godric Gryffindor",s:"The founder of Gryffindor",
 p:[`One of the four wizards who founded [[hogwarts|Hogwarts]] around the year 990. The [[chapeu|Sorting Hat]]'s song says he came from the moors. The village of [[godrics|Godric's Hollow]], where he was born, bears his name.`,
 `He wanted the brave in his house, and argued that the school should accept any child with magic, wherever they came from. He was the best friend of [[salazar|Salazar Slytherin]] until the quarrel over Muggle-borns, which ended with Slytherin's departure.`,
 `He left two objects that still act in the story. The Sorting Hat was his hat, and the four founders put a little of their intelligence into it so that the Sorting would go on after they died. The [[espada|Sword of Gryffindor]] appears to any [[grifinoria|Gryffindor]] student who truly needs it.`],
 f:[["Period","10th century"],["Origin","Godric's Hollow, in south-west England"],["House","Gryffindor"]],
 x:[["site","He was the most skilled duellist of his time and fought against discrimination towards Muggle-borns."],["site","The sword was made by Ragnuk the First, king of the goblins and the finest goldsmith of the day. Ragnuk later claimed it had been stolen, and the goblins maintain that version."]]},
salazar:{t:"figura",g:"The founders",c:"sons",n:"Salazar Slytherin",s:"The founder of Slytherin",
 p:[`According to the [[chapeu|Sorting Hat]], he came from the fens. He was a [[ofidioglossia|Parselmouth]], able to speak to snakes, a rare gift that he passed on to his descendants. Hence the serpent of [[sonserina|Slytherin]].`,
 `He distrusted students from Muggle families at a time when wizards were being persecuted, and wanted the school only for those of wizarding blood. He lost the argument to [[godrico|Gryffindor]] and left Hogwarts. Before going, he built the [[camara|Chamber of Secrets]] and locked a [[basilisco|basilisk]] inside it, so that his heir would one day open it and rid the school of Muggle-borns.`,
 `His last known descendants are [[gaunt|the Gaunts]], and the last of them is Tom Riddle, [[voldemort|Lord Voldemort]]. Slytherin's locket, a family heirloom, became one of the [[horcruxes|Horcruxes]].`],
 f:[["Period","10th century"],["Origin","The fens of eastern England"],["House","Slytherin"],["Gift","Parseltongue"]],
 x:[["site","He was also a talented Legilimens."],["site","His wand, with a basilisk-horn core, was taken to America by Isolt Sayre. Buried on the grounds of [[ilvermorny|Ilvermorny]], it grew into a tree whose leaves have healing power."]]},
rowena:{t:"figura",g:"The founders",c:"corv",n:"Rowena Ravenclaw",s:"The founder of Ravenclaw",
 p:[`She came from the glens of Scotland, according to the [[chapeu|Sorting Hat]], and was the brightest witch of her time. She wanted the sharpest minds in [[corvinal|Ravenclaw]]. She was the best friend of [[helga|Helga Hufflepuff]].`,
 `She wore a diadem that was said to increase the wisdom of whoever put it on. Her daughter Helena, jealous of her mother, stole the diadem and fled to Albania. Rowena fell ill and hid the theft from the other founders. She sent a baron who loved her after her daughter. Helena refused him, he killed her in a fit of rage and then killed himself.`,
 `The two returned to Hogwarts as ghosts: the Grey Lady and the Bloody Baron. Centuries later, Tom Riddle wrung the diadem's hiding place out of Helena and made it a [[horcruxes|Horcrux]].`],
 f:[["Period","10th century"],["Origin","Scotland"],["House","Ravenclaw"]],
 x:[["site","Hogwarts' name and location are said to have come from her: she dreamed of a warty hog that led her to a cliff at the edge of a lake."],["site","The staircases and floors that change places are attributed to her."]]},
helga:{t:"figura",g:"The founders",c:"lufa",n:"Helga Hufflepuff",s:"The founder of Hufflepuff",
 p:[`She came from the wide valleys of Wales, according to the [[chapeu|Sorting Hat]]. Of the four, she was the only one who set no conditions: she would teach all those the others did not want, and she would teach everything she knew.`,
 `She left a small golden cup with two handles and an engraved badger. The cup stayed in the family until it reached Hepzibah Smith, a wealthy collector. Tom Riddle killed her to get the cup and Slytherin's locket, and made both of them [[horcruxes|Horcruxes]].`],
 f:[["Period","10th century"],["Origin","Wales"],["House","Hufflepuff"]],
 x:[["site","She was a specialist in food-related charms. Many of the recipes for Hogwarts feasts come from her."],["site","It was Helga who brought the [[elfos|house-elves]] to the castle kitchens, so that they would have a safe place and work without ill-treatment."]]},

/* ---------- CHARACTERS ---------- */
harry:{t:"figura",g:"The trio",c:"grif",n:"Harry Potter",s:"The Boy Who Lived",
 p:[`Born on 31 July 1980, the son of [[tiagolilian|James and Lily Potter]]. A [[profecia|prophecy]] announced that a boy born at the end of July would have the power to defeat [[voldemort|Voldemort]]. On 31 October 1981 Voldemort killed his parents in [[godrics|Godric's Hollow]]. The Killing Curse cast at the baby rebounded on Voldemort himself, thanks to [[amor|Lily's sacrifice]], and left Harry with the lightning-bolt scar.`,
 `He grew up with [[dursley|the Dursleys]], knowing nothing of this. At eleven he entered [[hogwarts|Hogwarts]] and [[grifinoria|Gryffindor]], became the youngest Seeker in a century and, year after year, faced Voldemort's attempts to return. He is a [[ofidioglossia|Parselmouth]] and has a mental link with his enemy because, without either of them knowing it, he carried a piece of Voldemort's soul: he was the [[horcruxes|Horcrux]] that Voldemort never meant to make.`,
 `In 1997 he set out with [[rony|Ron]] and [[hermione|Hermione]] to hunt the Horcruxes. In the Battle of Hogwarts, on 2 May 1998, he gave himself up to die, came back, and defeated Voldemort with a Disarming Charm. He is descended from Ignotus Peverell and is the only one to have united all three [[reliquias|Deathly Hallows]].`],
 f:[["Born","31 July 1980"],["House","Gryffindor"],["Wand","Holly and phoenix feather, 11 inches (28 cm)"],["Patronus","Stag"],["Owl","Hedwig"]],
 x:[["ent","After the war he joined the [[aurores|Aurors]] and, in 2007, became head of the department. He married [[gina|Ginny Weasley]] and they had three children: James Sirius, Albus Severus and Lily Luna."],["ent","He lost his Parseltongue when the piece of Voldemort's soul was destroyed."],["site","The Potter family descends from Linfred of Stinchcombe, a 12th-century wizard who brewed potions. Harry's grandfather, Fleamont Potter, made his fortune with a hair potion."],["peca","In 2020 he is Head of the Department of Magical Law Enforcement."]]},
rony:{t:"figura",g:"The trio",c:"grif",n:"Ron Weasley",s:"Ronald Bilius Weasley",
 p:[`The sixth of the seven children of the [[weasley|Weasley family]], born on 1 March 1980. He met [[harry|Harry]] on the Hogwarts Express and was never apart from him for long again. He grew up in the shadow of five older brothers, and almost everything that drives or holds him back comes from that.`,
 `He plays wizard's chess very well, was Keeper for [[grifinoria|Gryffindor]] and is terrified of spiders. He abandoned the Horcrux hunt under the influence of the locket, came back guided by [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]]'s Deluminator and destroyed the locket with the [[espada|sword]]. He married [[hermione|Hermione]], and their children are called Rose and Hugo.`],
 f:[["Born","1 March 1980"],["House","Gryffindor"],["Patronus","Jack Russell terrier"]],
 x:[["ent","He worked with George at Weasleys' Wizard Wheezes and was also an Auror alongside Harry."]]},
hermione:{t:"figura",g:"The trio",c:"grif",n:"Hermione Granger",s:"The brightest witch of her age",
 p:[`The daughter of two Muggle dentists, she was born on 19 September 1979. She is the top student of her year and living proof against the [[sangue|pure-blood]] theory. Without her, [[harry|Harry]] and [[rony|Ron]] would not have made it past their first year.`,
 `She founded S.P.E.W., a society for the liberation of [[elfos|house-elves]], used a [[viratempo|Time-Turner]] to attend every class in third year and helped create [[armada|Dumbledore's Army]]. Before the Horcrux hunt, she erased herself from her parents' memories and sent them to Australia to protect them.`],
 f:[["Born","19 September 1979"],["House","Gryffindor"],["Wand","Vine wood and dragon heartstring"],["Patronus","Otter"],["Cat","Crookshanks, part Kneazle"]],
 x:[["ent","She restored her parents' memories, went back to Hogwarts to finish her seventh year and built a career at the [[ministerio|Ministry]]: first improving the lives of house-elves, then in Magical Law Enforcement, where she overturned the laws favouring pure-bloods."],["peca","In 2019 she becomes Minister for Magic."]]},
dumbledore:{t:"figura",g:"Hogwarts",c:"grif",n:"Albus Dumbledore",s:"Headmaster of Hogwarts",
 p:[`Albus Percival Wulfric Brian Dumbledore was born in 1881. His father was sent to [[azkaban|Azkaban]] for attacking three Muggle boys who had hurt his daughter, [[aberforth|Ariana]]. A brilliant [[grifinoria|Gryffindor]] student, Albus had to return home in 1899, when his mother died, to look after his siblings.`,
 `That summer he became friends with [[grindelwald|Gellert Grindelwald]]. The two dreamed of the [[reliquias|Deathly Hallows]] and of a world ruled by wizards 'for the greater good'. A three-way fight with Aberforth ended with Ariana dead, and Dumbledore never knew whose spell it was. He came to distrust himself with power in his hands and repeatedly turned down the post of Minister.`,
 `He defeated Grindelwald in 1945 and took the Elder Wand. As a professor, he went to fetch Tom Riddle from the orphanage. As headmaster, he founded the [[ordem|Order of the Phoenix]] and prepared [[harry|Harry]] for the war. In 1996 he put on the Gaunt ring, which was a Horcrux, and the curse gave him a year to live. He arranged his own death with [[snape|Snape]], who killed him at the top of the Astronomy Tower on 30 June 1997.`],
 f:[["Life","1881 to 1997"],["House","Gryffindor"],["Wand","The Elder Wand, from 1945 to 1997"],["Phoenix","Fawkes"]],
 x:[["ent","In October 2007, at Carnegie Hall, the author said she had always thought of Dumbledore as gay and in love with Grindelwald."],["ent","In the Mirror of Erised he saw his whole family together and reconciled, not a pair of socks."],["af","The films show a blood pact made in their youth, which prevented the two from fighting each other, and Dumbledore acting against Grindelwald through [[newt|Newt Scamander]]."]]},
mcgonagall:{t:"figura",g:"Hogwarts",c:"grif",n:"Minerva McGonagall",s:"Transfiguration professor",
 p:[`Deputy headmistress of Hogwarts, head of [[grifinoria|Gryffindor]] and a registered [[animagos|Animagus]], able to turn into a tabby cat. Strict, fair and passionate about [[quadribol|Quidditch]]: she was the one who put [[harry|Harry]] on the team in his first year.`,
 `She stood up to [[umbridge|Umbridge]] inside the school, led the defence of the castle in the Battle of Hogwarts and became headmistress after the war.`],
 f:[["House","Gryffindor"],["Animagus form","Tabby cat"]],
 x:[["site","Born on 4 October 1935 in the Scottish Highlands, the daughter of a witch and a Muggle Presbyterian minister. She turned down her Muggle fiancé, Dougal McGregor, so as not to have to hide her magic the way her mother did."],["site","She worked at the Ministry for two years before starting to teach at Hogwarts in December 1956. She married late, to Elphinstone Urquart, her former boss."]]},
snape:{t:"figura",g:"Hogwarts",c:"sons",n:"Severus Snape",s:"Potions Master and double agent",
 p:[`The son of a witch and a Muggle, he grew up poor in Spinner's End, a neighbour of Lily Evans, whom he loved all his life. At Hogwarts he was the target of the [[marotos|Marauders]]' cruel pranks. He invented spells while still at school and signed himself the Half-Blood Prince.`,
 `He joined the [[comensais|Death Eaters]] and it was he who carried the [[profecia|prophecy]] to [[voldemort|Voldemort]]. When he saw that it condemned Lily, he went to [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] and began spying for him. After her death, he swore to protect her son.`,
 `For sixteen years he made both sides believe he was theirs. He killed Dumbledore at the headmaster's own request, ran Hogwarts under Voldemort's regime protecting the students as best he could and brought the [[espada|sword]] to [[harry|Harry]]. He was killed by Nagini in the Shrieking Shack on 2 May 1998, and gave Harry the memories that explained everything.`],
 f:[["Life","9 January 1960 to 2 May 1998"],["House","Slytherin"],["Patronus","Doe, like Lily's"]],
 x:[["ent","Harry made sure Snape's portrait was placed in the headmaster's office."]]},
hagrid:{t:"figura",g:"Hogwarts",c:"grif",n:"Rubeus Hagrid",s:"Keeper of Keys and Grounds at Hogwarts",
 p:[`The son of a wizard and the [[gigantes|giantess]] Fridwulfa. He was expelled in his third year, in 1943, after Tom Riddle accused him of opening the [[camara|Chamber of Secrets]], when the creature he was secretly raising was only Aragog, an [[acromantula|Acromantula]]. [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] kept him at the school as gamekeeper.`,
 `He was the one who took [[harry|Harry]] out of the ruins of Godric's Hollow and the one who told him, ten years later, that he was a wizard. He has a soft spot for any creature with fangs: he raised the dragon Norbert, the three-headed dog Fluffy and the [[explosivim|Blast-Ended Skrewts]]. He began teaching Care of Magical Creatures in 1993.`],
 f:[["Born","6 December 1928"],["House","Gryffindor"],["Half-brother","Grawp, a giant"]],
 x:[["ent","He cannot conjure a Patronus. He stayed on at Hogwarts after the war."]]},
voldemort:{t:"figura",g:"The Dark Side",c:"trevas",n:"Lord Voldemort",s:"Tom Marvolo Riddle, You-Know-Who",
 p:[`Born on 31 December 1926 in a London orphanage. His mother, Merope [[gaunt|Gaunt]], a descendant of [[salazar|Slytherin]], had bewitched a rich Muggle, Tom Riddle, with a love potion. Abandoned, she died in childbirth. The name he invented later is an anagram of his birth name.`,
 `At [[hogwarts|Hogwarts]] he was a model student in [[sonserina|Slytherin]]. He opened the [[camara|Chamber of Secrets]] in 1943, killed his father and grandparents the same year and began splitting his soul into [[horcruxes|Horcruxes]] so as not to die. He gathered the [[comensais|Death Eaters]] and, from 1970, launched a war to put pure-bloods in charge.`,
 `He fell in 1981 when he tried to kill [[harry|Harry]]. He spent thirteen years without a body, returned in June 1995 in a ritual using the boy's blood, took over the [[ministerio|Ministry]] in 1997 and died on 2 May 1998, when his own curse rebounded on him a second time. The [[reliquias|Elder Wand]] he wielded was loyal to Harry.`],
 f:[["Life","31 December 1926 to 2 May 1998"],["House","Slytherin"],["Wand","Yew and phoenix feather, twin to Harry's"],["Snake","Nagini"]],
 x:[["ent","Because he was conceived under a love potion, the author describes him as incapable of understanding love. His Boggart would be his own corpse."],["peca","The play gives him a daughter with [[belatriz|Bellatrix Lestrange]]: [[delphi|Delphi]]."]]},
belatriz:{t:"figura",g:"The Dark Side",c:"trevas",n:"Bellatrix Lestrange",s:"The most faithful Death Eater",
 p:[`Born a Black, cousin of [[sirius|Sirius]] and sister of Narcissa [[malfoy|Malfoy]] and of Andromeda, [[tonks|Tonks]]'s mother. Devoted to [[voldemort|Voldemort]] to the point of obsession. With her husband, her brother-in-law and Barty Crouch Jr., she tortured [[neville|Neville]]'s parents into madness.`,
 `She escaped from [[azkaban|Azkaban]] in 1996. She killed Sirius in the [[misterios|Department of Mysteries]] and [[dobby|Dobby]] during the escape from Malfoy Manor. She died in the Battle of Hogwarts, in a duel with Molly [[weasley|Weasley]].`],
 f:[["House","Slytherin"],["Family","Black, married to Rodolphus Lestrange"]]},
pettigrew:{t:"figura",g:"The Dark Side",c:"trevas",n:"Peter Pettigrew",s:"Wormtail",
 p:[`The fourth of the [[marotos|Marauders]], an [[animagos|Animagus]] who took the form of a rat. He was the Potters' Secret-Keeper in the [[fidelius|Fidelius Charm]] and betrayed them to [[voldemort|Voldemort]]. Cornered by [[sirius|Sirius]], he blew up the street, killed twelve Muggles, cut off a finger and vanished, leaving his friend to take the blame.`,
 `He lived for twelve years as Scabbers, the [[weasley|Weasley family]]'s rat. Unmasked in 1994, he fled and helped Voldemort regain a body, giving his own hand in the ritual. The silver hand he received in return strangled him when he hesitated to kill [[harry|Harry]].`],
 f:[["House","Gryffindor"],["Animagus form","Rat"]]},
malfoy:{t:"figura",g:"The Dark Side",c:"sons",n:"The Malfoys",s:"Lucius, Narcissa and Draco",
 p:[`A rich, old [[sangue|pure-blood]] family. Lucius was a [[comensais|Death Eater]], escaped Azkaban in 1981 by claiming he had acted under the Imperius Curse and kept his influence at the [[ministerio|Ministry]]. It was he who slipped Riddle's diary into [[gina|Ginny]]'s cauldron.`,
 `Draco is [[harry|Harry]]'s rival at school. At sixteen he was ordered by [[voldemort|Voldemort]] to kill [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]], as punishment for his father's failure. He disarmed the headmaster and could go no further. With that act he became, unknowingly, the master of the [[reliquias|Elder Wand]], until Harry disarmed him months later.`,
 `Narcissa lied to Voldemort in the Forbidden Forest, saying Harry was dead, so that she could enter the castle and look for her son. That lie spared the family from Azkaban.`],
 f:[["House","Slytherin"],["Draco's wand","Hawthorn and unicorn hair"]],
 x:[["ent","Draco married Astoria Greengrass and raised his son, Scorpius, away from the ideas he himself was raised with."],["site","The Malfoys came to England with William the Conqueror and moved among Muggle nobility until the Statute of Secrecy."]]},
grindelwald:{t:"figura",g:"The Dark Side",c:"trevas",n:"Gellert Grindelwald",s:"The dark wizard before Voldemort",
 p:[`Expelled from [[escolas|Durmstrang]], he ended up in [[godrics|Godric's Hollow]] in the summer of 1899, at the house of his great-aunt Bathilda Bagshot, next to the grave of Ignotus Peverell. There he met [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]]. The motto 'for the greater good' was born in the letters between the two.`,
 `He stole the [[reliquias|Elder Wand]] from the wandmaker Gregorovitch and raised a movement for wizard dominion over Muggles across Europe. Dumbledore defeated him in 1945. He was held in [[nurmengard|Nurmengard]], the fortress he had built himself, until [[voldemort|Voldemort]] killed him in 1998 for refusing to say where the wand was.`],
 f:[["Life","c. 1883 to 1998"],["School","Durmstrang"],["Symbol","The sign of the Deathly Hallows"]],
 x:[["af","The films tell of his rise: in 1926 he operates in New York disguised as Percival Graves of [[macusa|MACUSA]]. In 1927 he escapes and gathers followers in Paris. In the early 1930s he tries to rig the election of the [[confederacao|International Confederation of Wizards]]."],["af","He is a seer, and uses visions of the Muggle world war to win wizards over."]]},
sirius:{t:"figura",g:"The Order",c:"grif",n:"Sirius Black",s:"Padfoot, Harry's godfather",
 p:[`The heir to a family obsessed with [[sangue|pure blood]], he was the first Black in [[grifinoria|Gryffindor]] and ran away from home at sixteen to live with the Potters. An [[animagos|Animagus]] in the form of a large black dog, one of the [[marotos|Marauders]].`,
 `He spent twelve years in [[azkaban|Azkaban]] without a trial, for the betrayal and the murders that [[pettigrew|Pettigrew]] committed. He escaped in 1993, the first to manage it, swimming in dog form. He lived as a fugitive, lent the family house at [[grimmauld|Grimmauld Place]] to the [[ordem|Order of the Phoenix]] and died in the [[misterios|Department of Mysteries]] in June 1996, falling through the veil.`],
 f:[["Life","3 November 1959 to 18 June 1996"],["House","Gryffindor"],["Animagus form","Black dog"]]},
lupin:{t:"figura",g:"The Order",c:"grif",n:"Remus Lupin",s:"Moony, professor and werewolf",
 p:[`Bitten as a child by Fenrir Greyback, he was only able to study because [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] planted the Whomping Willow to hide the passage to the [[gritos|Shrieking Shack]], where he transformed. His friends became [[animagos|Animagi]] to keep him company on full moons. That is how the [[marotos|Marauders]] came to be.`,
 `He was the best Defence Against the Dark Arts teacher [[harry|Harry]] ever had, and the one who taught him the [[patrono|Patronus]]. He married [[tonks|Tonks]], and the two died in the Battle of Hogwarts, weeks after the birth of their son, Teddy.`],
 f:[["Life","10 March 1960 to 2 May 1998"],["House","Gryffindor"]],
 x:[["site","His father, Lyall Lupin, had offended Greyback at a Ministry hearing. The bite on his son, shortly before he turned five, was revenge."],["ent","The author describes Lupin's lycanthropy as a metaphor for illnesses that carry a stigma."]]},
tiagolilian:{t:"figura",g:"The Order",c:"grif",n:"James and Lily Potter",s:"Harry's parents",
 p:[`James was the only child of a rich wizarding family, a Chaser for [[grifinoria|Gryffindor]], an [[animagos|Animagus]] in the form of a stag, the Prongs of the [[marotos|Marauders]]. Lily Evans was Muggle-born, the sister of Petunia [[dursley|Dursley]], [[slughorn|Slughorn]]'s best Potions student and a childhood friend of [[snape|Snape]], until he called her a Mudblood.`,
 `Both joined the [[ordem|Order of the Phoenix]] and escaped [[voldemort|Voldemort]] three times. They hid under the [[fidelius|Fidelius Charm]] and were betrayed by [[pettigrew|Pettigrew]]. James died without a wand, trying to buy time. Lily could have saved herself and chose to stand between Voldemort and her son. That choice is the [[amor|protection]] that brought Voldemort down.`],
 f:[["Death","31 October 1981, in Godric's Hollow"],["James","Born on 27 March 1960"],["Lily","Born on 30 January 1960"]]},
marotos:{t:"figura",g:"The Order",c:"grif",n:"The Marauders",s:"Moony, Wormtail, Padfoot and Prongs",
 p:[`The group of [[grifinoria|Gryffindor]] friends from the 1970s: [[lupin|Remus Lupin]], [[pettigrew|Peter Pettigrew]], [[sirius|Sirius Black]] and [[tiagolilian|James Potter]]. Three of them became illegal [[animagos|Animagi]] to keep Lupin company on full-moon nights.`,
 `Those outings gave rise to the [[mapa|Marauder's Map]], which shows the whole castle and everyone moving around in it. They were brilliant, popular and, with [[snape|Snape]], cruel. All four died because of the war.`]},
weasley:{t:"figura",g:"The Order",c:"grif",n:"The Weasley family",s:"Arthur, Molly and the seven children",
 p:[`A [[sangue|pure-blood]] family branded 'blood traitors' for liking Muggles. Arthur works at the [[ministerio|Ministry]], in the Misuse of Muggle Artefacts Office. Molly looks after [[toca|The Burrow]] and, in practice, adopts [[harry|Harry]].`,
 `The children: Bill, a curse-breaker at [[gringotes|Gringotts]], married to Fleur Delacour. Charlie, who studies dragons in Romania. Percy, who breaks with the family to side with the Ministry and returns in the final battle. The twins Fred and George, founders of Weasleys' Wizard Wheezes. [[rony|Ron]] and [[gina|Ginny]].`,
 `Fred died in the Battle of Hogwarts. All the adult Weasleys were in the [[ordem|Order of the Phoenix]].`],
 f:[["House","Gryffindor, all of them"],["Home","The Burrow, near Ottery St Catchpole"]],
 x:[["ent","George kept the shop going, married Angelina Johnson and named their first child Fred."],["site","The Weasleys are among the 'Sacred Twenty-Eight', the list of pure-blood families published in the 1930s, and protested at being included."]]},
gina:{t:"figura",g:"The Order",c:"grif",n:"Ginny Weasley",s:"Ginevra Weasley",
 p:[`The youngest and only girl of the [[weasley|Weasley family]]. In her first year she was possessed by Tom Riddle's diary, a [[horcruxes|Horcrux]], and opened the [[camara|Chamber of Secrets]] without knowing what she was doing.`,
 `She grew into one of the most powerful witches of her year: Chaser and Seeker for [[grifinoria|Gryffindor]], a member of [[armada|Dumbledore's Army]], and leader of the resistance inside Hogwarts in 1997 alongside [[neville|Neville]] and [[luna|Luna]]. She married [[harry|Harry]].`],
 f:[["Born","11 August 1981"],["House","Gryffindor"]],
 x:[["ent","She played professionally for the Holyhead Harpies and then became the Daily Prophet's [[quadribol|Quidditch]] correspondent."],["site","She is the one who writes the coverage of the 2014 World Cup in the author's texts."]]},
neville:{t:"figura",g:"Hogwarts",c:"grif",n:"Neville Longbottom",s:"The other boy of the prophecy",
 p:[`Born on 30 July 1980, a day before [[harry|Harry]], and the [[profecia|prophecy]] could apply to either of them. [[voldemort|Voldemort]] chose Harry. Neville's parents, both Aurors, were tortured by [[belatriz|Bellatrix Lestrange]] until they lost their sanity, and he was raised by his grandmother.`,
 `He starts the story as the clumsy student and ends it as a leader of the resistance at Hogwarts. In the final battle he pulled the [[espada|Sword of Gryffindor]] from the Sorting Hat and killed Nagini, the last [[horcruxes|Horcrux]].`],
 f:[["Born","30 July 1980"],["House","Gryffindor"]],
 x:[["ent","He became a Herbology professor at Hogwarts and married Hannah Abbott, who took over the Leaky Cauldron."]]},
luna:{t:"figura",g:"Hogwarts",c:"corv",n:"Luna Lovegood",s:"The girl who believes in what no one else sees",
 p:[`The daughter of Xenophilius Lovegood, editor of The Quibbler. She saw her mother die in an experimental spell, which is why she can see [[testralio|Thestrals]]. In [[corvinal|Ravenclaw]] she is treated as odd. She is also the one who says the most lucid things when [[harry|Harry]] needs to hear them.`,
 `She fought in the [[misterios|Department of Mysteries]], was kidnapped from the Hogwarts Express and held in the cellar of Malfoy Manor, and fought in the Battle of Hogwarts.`],
 f:[["Born","13 February 1981"],["House","Ravenclaw"]],
 x:[["ent","She became a naturalist, discovered and classified new species and married Rolf Scamander, [[newt|Newt]]'s grandson."]]},
cedrico:{t:"figura",g:"Hogwarts",c:"lufa",n:"Cedric Diggory",s:"The Hogwarts champion",
 p:[`Seeker and captain of [[lufalufa|Hufflepuff]], chosen by the Goblet of Fire for the 1994 [[tribruxo|Triwizard Tournament]]. He reached the cup together with [[harry|Harry]], and the two decided to touch it at the same time. It was a Portkey. In the Little Hangleton graveyard, [[pettigrew|Pettigrew]] killed him on [[voldemort|Voldemort]]'s orders, on 24 June 1995.`,
 `He is the first death of the second war, and the one the [[ministerio|Ministry]] spent a year denying.`],
 f:[["House","Hufflepuff"],["Death","24 June 1995"]]},
moody:{t:"figura",g:"The Order",c:"pedra",n:"Alastor Moody",s:"Mad-Eye",
 p:[`The most famous [[aurores|Auror]] of the first war: he filled half the cells in [[azkaban|Azkaban]] himself. He lost a leg, an eye and part of his nose. The magical eye he wears sees through walls and Invisibility Cloaks.`,
 `In 1994 he was kidnapped by Barty [[crouch|Crouch]] Jr., who took his place at Hogwarts for a whole year with Polyjuice Potion. He died in July 1997, in the operation of the seven Potters.`]},
tonks:{t:"figura",g:"The Order",c:"lufa",n:"Nymphadora Tonks",s:"Auror and Metamorphmagus",
 p:[`The daughter of Andromeda Black, disowned by the family for marrying a Muggle-born. She is a [[metamorfomagos|Metamorphmagus]]: she changes her appearance at will, with neither potion nor spell. She qualified as an [[aurores|Auror]] under [[moody|Moody]] and joined the [[ordem|Order of the Phoenix]].`,
 `She married [[lupin|Lupin]] in 1997. The two died in the Battle of Hogwarts. Their son, Teddy, was raised by his grandmother, with [[harry|Harry]] as godfather.`],
 f:[["House","Hufflepuff"]]},
kingsley:{t:"figura",g:"The Order",c:"pedra",n:"Kingsley Shacklebolt",s:"Auror and Minister",
 p:[`An [[aurores|Auror]] of the [[ordem|Order of the Phoenix]]. He even worked in the Muggle prime minister's office to protect him. After the Battle of Hogwarts he was appointed Minister for Magic.`],
 x:[["ent","He stayed in the post and reformed the [[ministerio|Ministry]]. He removed the [[dementadores|Dementors]] from [[azkaban|Azkaban]]."],["site","The Shacklebolts also appear among the 'Sacred Twenty-Eight'."]]},
umbridge:{t:"figura",g:"The Ministry",c:"trevas",n:"Dolores Umbridge",s:"Senior Undersecretary to the Minister",
 p:[`Sent by the [[ministerio|Ministry]] to Hogwarts in 1995 to silence [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] and [[harry|Harry]]. As High Inquisitor, she issued decrees, banned the practice of defensive spells and made students write with a quill that cuts the words into their own hand.`,
 `It was she who sent the [[dementadores|Dementors]] after Harry. Under [[voldemort|Voldemort]]'s regime, she headed the commission that took away the wands of Muggle-borns, wearing Slytherin's locket round her neck.`],
 x:[["ent","After the war she was tried and imprisoned for crimes against Muggle-borns."],["site","The daughter of a wizard and a Muggle, she hid her origins and claimed to be a pure-blood."]]},
fudge:{t:"figura",g:"The Ministry",c:"pedra",n:"Cornelius Fudge",s:"Minister for Magic from 1990 to 1996",
 p:[`A well-meaning and weak Minister who at first asked [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] for advice every week. When [[voldemort|Voldemort]] returned, in 1995, he preferred not to believe it. He used the Daily Prophet to paint [[harry|Harry]] as a liar and Dumbledore as senile, and lost a whole year of preparation.`,
 `He fell in 1996, after half the [[ministerio|Ministry]] saw Voldemort in the Atrium. He was replaced by Rufus Scrimgeour, killed by the [[comensais|Death Eaters]] in the coup of 1 August 1997.`]},
crouch:{t:"figura",g:"The Ministry",c:"pedra",n:"Barty Crouch, father and son",s:"The judge and the Death Eater",
 p:[`Bartemius Crouch headed Magical Law Enforcement during the first war. He authorised the [[aurores|Aurors]] to use the [[imperdoaveis|Unforgivable Curses]] and sent people to [[azkaban|Azkaban]] without trial, [[sirius|Sirius Black]] among them. He was on his way to becoming Minister when his own son was caught among the torturers of the Longbottoms. He condemned his son in public.`,
 `The mother, ill, swapped places with the boy in Azkaban and died there. The father kept him at home under the Imperius Curse for years. Crouch Jr. escaped, took [[moody|Moody]]'s place at Hogwarts, put [[harry|Harry]]'s name in the Goblet of Fire and killed his father. He ended up with his soul sucked out by a [[dementadores|Dementor]].`]},
slughorn:{t:"figura",g:"Hogwarts",c:"sons",n:"Horace Slughorn",s:"Potions Master and collector of talent",
 p:[`Head of [[sonserina|Slytherin]] before and after [[snape|Snape]]. He collects promising students in the Slug Club. It was to him that the young Tom Riddle asked about [[horcruxes|Horcruxes]] and about splitting the soul into seven. The shame of that conversation made him tamper with his own memory.`,
 `[[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] brought him out of retirement in 1996 precisely so that [[harry|Harry]] could get the true memory. In the Battle of Hogwarts he came back with reinforcements and duelled Voldemort.`]},
lockhart:{t:"figura",g:"Hogwarts",c:"corv",n:"Gilderoy Lockhart",s:"Famous writer and fraud",
 p:[`Defence Against the Dark Arts professor in 1992. The adventure books that made him famous tell of the deeds of other wizards, whose memories he wiped. He is genuinely good at only one thing, the Memory Charm.`,
 `He tried to use it on [[harry|Harry]] and [[rony|Ron]] in the [[camara|Chamber of Secrets]] with Ron's broken wand. The spell backfired, and he has lived ever since in the permanent spell damage ward at [[mungus|St Mungo's]].`],
 x:[["ent","The author said he never recovered."]]},
dobby:{t:"figura",g:"Allies",c:"pedra",n:"Dobby",s:"A free elf",
 p:[`The [[elfos|house-elf]] of the [[malfoy|Malfoys]]. He tried to stop [[harry|Harry]] from going back to Hogwarts in 1992 to protect him from Lucius's plan. Harry freed him by tricking his master, who handed him a sock.`,
 `He went to work in the Hogwarts kitchens, paid, which scandalised the other elves. In 1998 he got the prisoners out of the cellar of Malfoy Manor and died with [[belatriz|Bellatrix]]'s knife in his chest. Harry dug the grave by hand, near [[conchas|Shell Cottage]].`]},
dursley:{t:"figura",g:"The Muggles",c:"pedra",n:"The Dursleys",s:"Vernon, Petunia and Dudley",
 p:[`[[harry|Harry]]'s aunt, uncle and cousin, who live at [[alfeneiros|4 Privet Drive]]. Petunia is Lily's sister and spent her life angry at the world her sister entered and she did not. They raised Harry in the cupboard under the stairs, hiding from him that he was a wizard.`,
 `The house was safe because of [[amor|Lily's blood]] running in Petunia. As long as Harry could call that place home, [[voldemort|Voldemort]] could not reach him there. Dudley says goodbye to his cousin in 1997 with an awkward thank-you.`],
 x:[["site","Petunia wrote to Dumbledore as a child, asking to go to Hogwarts with her sister."],["ent","Harry and Dudley kept in touch as adults, enough for a Christmas card."]]},
gaunt:{t:"figura",g:"Family lines",c:"sons",n:"The Gaunts",s:"The last descendants of Slytherin",
 p:[`A [[sangue|pure-blood]] family descended from [[salazar|Salazar Slytherin]] and from the [[peverell|Peverells]]. They squandered their fortune generations earlier and married cousins to cousins until all that was left was a hovel in Little Hangleton, the gift of [[ofidioglossia|Parseltongue]] and two heirlooms: Slytherin's locket and a ring with the Resurrection Stone.`,
 `In the 1920s Marvolo and his children, Morfin and Merope, remained. Merope ran off with the Muggle Tom Riddle and died giving birth to the future [[voldemort|Voldemort]]. In 1943 the boy sought out his uncle, killed the Riddles with his wand and let him take the blame. He kept the ring, which became a [[horcruxes|Horcrux]].`],
 x:[["site","An Irish branch of the family appears in the story of [[ilvermorny|Ilvermorny]]: Gormlaith Gaunt, the aunt the founder fled from."]]},
peverell:{t:"figura",g:"Family lines",c:"pedra",n:"The Peverell brothers",s:"Antioch, Cadmus and Ignotus",
 p:[`Three wizard brothers of the 13th century, from [[godrics|Godric's Hollow]]. They are the three brothers of the tale in The Tales of Beedle the Bard, who were said to have received gifts from Death. [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] thought it more likely that they had made the [[reliquias|Deathly Hallows]] themselves.`,
 `Antioch took the Elder Wand and was murdered for it. Cadmus took the Resurrection Stone, which reached the [[gaunt|Gaunts]] and [[voldemort|Voldemort]]. Ignotus took the Invisibility Cloak, which passed from father to son down to [[harry|Harry]]. Harry and Voldemort are thus very distant relatives.`],
 x:[["site","Ignotus's granddaughter, Iolanthe Peverell, married Hardwin Potter. That is how the cloak entered the family."]]},
newt:{t:"figura",g:"Fantastic Beasts",c:"lufa",n:"Newt Scamander",s:"Newton Scamander, Magizoologist",
 p:[`Author of Fantastic Beasts and Where to Find Them, the textbook [[harry|Harry]] buys in his first year. Born in 1897, he was in [[lufalufa|Hufflepuff]] and worked at the [[ministerio|Ministry]], in the Department for the Regulation and Control of Magical Creatures. He travelled the world cataloguing species, and the book came out in 1927.`,
 `He appears on the Marauder's Map in 1993, and his grandson, Rolf, marries [[luna|Luna Lovegood]].`],
 f:[["Born","1897"],["House","Hufflepuff"],["Work","Fantastic Beasts and Where to Find Them, 1927"]],
 x:[["lt","The book's biography says he created the Werewolf Register in 1947, secured the ban on experimental breeding in 1965 and received the Order of Merlin, Second Class, in 1979."],["af","The films show him in New York in 1926, with a suitcase full of creatures, alongside Tina and Queenie Goldstein and the No-Maj Jacob Kowalski. Dumbledore uses him against [[grindelwald|Grindelwald]]. He was nearly expelled from Hogwarts for taking the blame for Leta Lestrange."]]},
credence:{t:"figura",g:"Fantastic Beasts",c:"trevas",n:"Credence Barebone",s:"The Obscurial of New York",
 p:[`A character from the Fantastic Beasts films. Raised in New York by a woman who preached against witches, he repressed his magic until it became an [[obscurus|Obscurus]], the force that devastated the city in 1926. He survived beyond the age at which Obscurials usually die.`,
 `[[grindelwald|Grindelwald]] lured him by saying he was a Dumbledore. The third film clarifies: he is Aurelius, the son of [[aberforth|Aberforth]].`],
 x:[["af","Everything known about him comes from the three films, with screenplays by the author."]]},
aberforth:{t:"figura",g:"The Order",c:"grif",n:"Aberforth and Ariana Dumbledore",s:"Albus's siblings",
 p:[`Ariana was attacked at the age of six by Muggle boys who saw her doing magic. She never controlled it again, and the magic exploded whenever she was upset. In one of these fits she accidentally killed her mother. She died in 1899, hit in the duel between her brothers and [[grindelwald|Grindelwald]].`,
 `Aberforth never forgave [[dumbledore|Albus]] and broke his nose at the funeral. He became the owner of the Hog's Head, in [[hogsmeade|Hogsmeade]]. It was he who sent [[dobby|Dobby]] to Malfoy Manor, and through the passage behind Ariana's portrait [[armada|the Army]] and [[ordem|the Order]] entered the castle for the final battle.`],
 x:[["af","The films suggest that Ariana's condition was that of an Obscurial."]]},
regulo:{t:"figura",g:"The Dark Side",c:"sons",n:"Regulus Black",s:"R.A.B.",
 p:[`[[sirius|Sirius]]'s younger brother, the son the family wanted. He joined the [[comensais|Death Eaters]] at sixteen. When [[voldemort|Voldemort]] used the family house-elf, Kreacher, to test the defences of the cave, and left him there to die, Regulus understood what the locket was.`,
 `He returned to the cave with Kreacher, drank the potion himself, swapped the locket for a fake and sent the elf away with the order to destroy the [[horcruxes|Horcrux]]. He was dragged into the lake by the [[inferi|Inferi]] in 1979, aged eighteen.`]},
flamel:{t:"figura",g:"Allies",c:"pedra",n:"Nicolas Flamel",s:"The alchemist",
 p:[`The only known maker of the [[pedrafilosofal|Philosopher's Stone]], a friend and study partner of [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]]. In 1991 he was 665 years old and lived with his wife, Perenelle, in Devon. After Quirrell's attack the two agreed to destroy the stone and, with the elixir that remained, put their affairs in order.`,
 `The name comes from a real person: a 14th-century Parisian scrivener to whom legend attributed the stone.`],
 x:[["af","He appears in Paris in 1927, in the second film."],["site","He was a student at [[escolas|Beauxbatons]]."]]},
olivaras:{t:"figura",g:"Allies",c:"corv",n:"Ollivander",s:"Garrick Ollivander, wandmaker",
 p:[`Owner of the shop in [[beco|Diagon Alley]], from the family that has made [[varinhas|wands]] since 382 BC. He remembers every wand he has sold. It was he who told [[harry|Harry]] that the feather in his wand and the one in [[voldemort|Voldemort]]'s came from the same phoenix.`,
 `Voldemort kidnapped him in 1996 to understand why the wand failed against Harry, and later to find out where the Elder Wand was. He was rescued from Malfoy Manor by [[dobby|Dobby]].`],
 x:[["site","It was he who reduced the cores to three, which he called the Supreme ones, and the long texts about wand woods on the official site are presented as his notes."]]},
trelawney:{t:"figura",g:"Hogwarts",c:"corv",n:"Sybill Trelawney",s:"Divination professor",
 p:[`The great-great-granddaughter of the seer Cassandra Trelawney and, almost all the time, a theatrical charlatan. She made two true [[profecia|prophecies]], which she does not remember: the one in 1980, about the boy who would defeat the Dark Lord, and the one in 1994, about the servant who would return to his master.`,
 `[[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] hired her after the first to keep her safe in the castle.`]},
delphi:{t:"figura",g:"After the war",c:"trevas",n:"Albus, Scorpius and Delphi",s:"The generation of The Cursed Child",
 p:[`Characters from the 2016 play. Albus Severus Potter, [[harry|Harry]]'s middle son, is sorted into [[sonserina|Slytherin]] and does not get along with his father. His best friend is Scorpius, son of Draco [[malfoy|Malfoy]], haunted by the rumour that he is Voldemort's son.`,
 `The two steal a [[viratempo|Time-Turner]] to save [[cedrico|Cedric Diggory]] and create ever worse timelines, one of them with [[voldemort|Voldemort]] victorious. The one manipulating them is Delphi, who turns out to be the daughter of Voldemort and [[belatriz|Bellatrix Lestrange]], born before the Battle of Hogwarts.`],
 x:[["peca","The whole story comes from Harry Potter and the Cursed Child, written by Jack Thorne from an original story by himself, the author and John Tiffany."]]},
merlin:{t:"figura",g:"Family lines",c:"sons",n:"Merlin",s:"The most famous wizard in history",
 p:[`In the world of Harry Potter, Merlin really existed and is the name wizards invoke when they are astonished. The [[ordemmerlin|Order of Merlin]], the greatest wizarding decoration, bears his name.`],
 x:[["site","He studied at Hogwarts, in [[sonserina|Slytherin]], and advocated coexistence with Muggles. The Order of Merlin began as an organisation that made rules against the use of magic on Muggles."]]},
krum:{t:"figura",g:"Hogwarts",c:"pedra",n:"Viktor Krum and Fleur Delacour",s:"The foreign champions",
 p:[`The other two champions of the 1994 [[tribruxo|Triwizard Tournament]]. Krum, from [[escolas|Durmstrang]], was already Bulgaria's Seeker in the final of that year's World Cup. He was [[hermione|Hermione]]'s date at the Yule Ball.`,
 `Fleur, from [[escolas|Beauxbatons]], has a [[veela|Veela]] grandmother. She joined the [[ordem|Order of the Phoenix]] and married Bill [[weasley|Weasley]] on 1 August 1997, the day the Ministry fell.`],
 x:[["site","Krum went back to playing and won the 2014 World Cup with Bulgaria, against Brazil."]]},
skeeter:{t:"figura",g:"The Ministry",c:"pedra",n:"Rita Skeeter",s:"Daily Prophet reporter",
 p:[`A scandal journalist armed with a Quick-Quotes Quill that writes by itself and exaggerates everything. She is an unregistered [[animagos|Animagus]], in the form of a beetle, which is how she overhears what she should not. [[hermione|Hermione]] found out and forced her to write the truth about [[voldemort|Voldemort]]'s return, published in The Quibbler.`,
 `After [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]]'s death she published a biography of him, full of venom and with several accurate facts.`]},
};
// mom: Ministry of Magic classification (X to XXXXX), when it exists.
Object.assign(E, {
/* ---------- BEINGS ---------- */
classificacao:{t:"criatura",g:"How the Ministry classifies",c:"magia",n:"Beings, beasts and spirits",s:"The three categories and the X to XXXXX scale",
 p:[`The [[ministerio|Ministry of Magic]] divides creatures into three groups. A Being is any creature intelligent enough to understand the laws of the magical community and to share the responsibility of making them. A Beast is everything else. A Spirit is the category created for [[fantasmas|ghosts]], who refused to be treated as living beings.`,
 `The definition took centuries. In the 14th century, Burdock Muldoon decided that a Being was whoever walked on two legs, and the goblins packed the meeting with trolls and imps. His successor, Elfrida Clagg, swapped the criterion for speech, and the trolls turned up taught to repeat phrases. The current definition is by Grogan Stump, Minister for Magic, in 1811.`,
 `[[centauros|Centaurs]] and [[sereianos|merpeople]] asked to be classified as Beasts, because they did not want to share a category with vampires and hags. [[lobisomens|Werewolves]] are Beings for almost the whole month and Beasts at the full moon. [[dementadores|Dementors]] and [[bichopapao|Boggarts]] fall outside everything: they are 'non-beings', which were never alive.`,
 `Among Beasts, [[newt|Newt Scamander]] records the Ministry's danger scale, which runs from X to XXXXX.`],
 br:[["X","Boring. Example: the Flobberworm."],["XX","Harmless, can be domesticated. Examples: Gnome, Bowtruckle."],["XXX","A competent wizard can cope. Examples: Hippogriff, Niffler."],["XXXX","Dangerous, requires specialist knowledge. Examples: Thestral, Unicorn, Phoenix."],["XXXXX","Known wizard-killer, impossible to train or domesticate. Examples: Basilisk, Dragon, Acromantula."]],bt:"The Ministry's scale",
 x:[["lt","All of this comes from the introduction to Fantastic Beasts and Where to Find Them. The Phoenix and the Unicorn are rated XXXX because they demand respect, not because they are aggressive."]]},
elfos:{t:"criatura",g:"Beings",c:"pedra",n:"House-elves",s:"Servants bound to a family",
 p:[`Small creatures with big ears and powerful magic of their own: they Apparate where wizards cannot, [[hogwarts|Hogwarts]] included, and do not use wands, which the law forbids them. They are bound to a house and a family, obliged to obey and to punish themselves when they disobey. They are free only if their master gives them an item of clothing.`,
 `Most consider freedom a disgrace, and that is what makes the issue difficult. [[dobby|Dobby]] wanted to be free. Winky, dismissed by the [[crouch|Crouches]], fell apart. Kreacher, of the Blacks, served [[regulo|Regulus]] with devotion and betrayed [[sirius|Sirius]], who despised him. More than a hundred elves work in the Hogwarts kitchens, the biggest concentration in Britain.`,
 `[[hermione|Hermione]] founded S.P.E.W. to free them. In the final battle, Kreacher led the Hogwarts elves against the [[comensais|Death Eaters]].`],
 f:[["Category","Being"]]},
duendes:{t:"criatura",g:"Beings",c:"pedra",n:"Goblins",s:"Bankers and goldsmiths",
 p:[`They run [[gringotes|Gringotts]] and a good part of the wizarding economy. They are peerless metalworkers: goblin-made silver repels dirt and absorbs only what strengthens it, which is why the [[espada|Sword of Gryffindor]] became imbued with basilisk venom.`,
 `They have a different idea of ownership. To a goblin, the owner of an object is whoever made it, and whoever buys it is only renting it for life. This, combined with the ban on carrying wands, fuelled centuries of rebellions, the dullest subject in Professor Binns's classes.`,
 `They speak Gobbledegook. The goblin Griphook helped [[harry|Harry]] break into Gringotts in exchange for the sword and betrayed him in the vault.`],
 f:[["Category","Being"],["Language","Gobbledegook"]]},
centauros:{t:"criatura",g:"Beings",c:"pedra",n:"Centaurs",s:"Astronomers of the Forbidden Forest",
 p:[`A horse's body, a human torso, intelligence equal to wizards' and no interest in them. They read the future in the stars and avoid interfering in what they see. A herd lives in the [[floresta|Forbidden Forest]].`,
 `Firenze broke the rule by carrying [[harry|Harry]] on his back and, later, by agreeing to teach Divination. He was driven out with kicks. In the Battle of Hogwarts the herd finally joined the fight.`],
 mom:"XXXX",f:[["Category","Beast, by their own choice"]],
 x:[["lt","The XXXX rating does not indicate aggression. It indicates that they must be treated with great respect."],["ent","Firenze was accepted back by the herd after the war."]]},
sereianos:{t:"criatura",g:"Beings",c:"pedra",n:"Merpeople",s:"The water people",
 p:[`They live in organised communities at the bottom of lakes and seas. The one in the [[hogwarts|Hogwarts]] lake was the setting for the second task of the [[tribruxo|Triwizard Tournament]]. They speak Mermish, which sounds like shrieking out of water. [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] spoke the language.`,
 `Those of warm waters resemble the mermaids of legend. Those of the Scottish lochs, the selkies, have grey skin and green hair.`],
 mom:"XXXX",f:[["Category","Beast, by their own choice"],["Language","Mermish"]]},
gigantes:{t:"criatura",g:"Beings",c:"pedra",n:"Giants",s:"A nearly extinct people",
 p:[`They stand over 20 feet (6 m) tall and resist most spells. Hunted by wizards and killing one another, only a few dozen remain, hidden in the mountains of eastern Europe. They fought for [[voldemort|Voldemort]] in both wars.`,
 `[[hagrid|Hagrid]] is the son of a giantess, as is Madame Maxime, headmistress of [[escolas|Beauxbatons]], who never admits it. The two were sent by [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] as ambassadors in 1995. Hagrid came back with his half-brother, Grawp.`],
 f:[["Category","Being"]]},
lobisomens:{t:"criatura",g:"Beings",c:"trevas",n:"Werewolves",s:"Humans who transform at the full moon",
 p:[`Lycanthropy is passed on by the bite of a transformed werewolf and has no cure. Outside the full moon the person is like anyone else. Transformed, they lose their reason and attack humans, preferably.`,
 `The Wolfsbane Potion, invented in the late 20th century by Damocles Belby, makes it possible to keep one's mind during the transformation. It is expensive and difficult. Prejudice does the rest: laws that bar werewolves from working push many into poverty and into the arms of people like Fenrir Greyback, who bites children on purpose and served [[voldemort|Voldemort]].`,
 `[[lupin|Remus Lupin]] is the case the books follow closely.`],
 mom:"XXXXX",f:[["Category","Being in human form, Beast when transformed"]]},
veela:{t:"criatura",g:"Beings",c:"pedra",n:"Veela",s:"Bewitching beauty",
 p:[`They look like women of supernatural beauty, and their dance leaves men beside themselves. When angry, they turn into beaked, scaly-winged creatures that throw balls of fire. They are the Bulgarian mascots at the 1994 [[quadribol|Quidditch]] World Cup.`,
 `Fleur [[krum|Delacour]]'s grandmother was a Veela, and one strand of her hair is the core of her granddaughter's [[varinhas|wand]].`],
 f:[["Category","Being"]]},
trasgos:{t:"criatura",g:"Beings",c:"pedra",n:"Trolls",s:"Enormous strength, hardly any brain",
 p:[`They reach 12 feet (4 m) in height and a ton in weight. There are three types: mountain, forest and river. Some learn a few isolated words and are used as guards.`,
 `The troll Quirrell let loose in the dungeons on Hallowe'en 1991 is what made [[harry|Harry]], [[rony|Ron]] and [[hermione|Hermione]] become friends.`],
 mom:"XXXX",f:[["Category","Beast, despite walking on two legs"]]},
vampiros:{t:"criatura",g:"Beings",c:"trevas",n:"Vampires and hags",s:"The beings others avoid",
 p:[`Vampires exist in the wizarding world and are classified as Beings, but they barely appear in the story: one of them, Sanguini, attends a party of [[slughorn|Slughorn]]'s. Hags look like old witches and are said to eat children.`,
 `It was the company of these two that made [[centauros|centaurs]] and [[sereianos|merpeople]] refuse the category of Beings.`],
 f:[["Category","Beings"]],
 x:[["site","The author said she once planned a vampire teacher for Hogwarts, named Trocar, and gave up on the idea."]]},

/* ---------- NON-BEINGS AND SPIRITS ---------- */
dementadores:{t:"criatura",g:"Non-beings and spirits",c:"trevas",n:"Dementors",s:"The guards of Azkaban",
 p:[`Hooded figures that feed on happiness. Near them everything grows cold and the person relives their worst memories. The Dementor's Kiss sucks the soul out through the mouth and leaves the body alive and empty. Muggles cannot see them, but feel the effect.`,
 `They do not die, they can only be driven off, and the only defence is the [[patrono|Patronus Charm]]. Chocolate helps afterwards. They guarded [[azkaban|Azkaban]] for centuries in the service of the [[ministerio|Ministry]] and went over to [[voldemort|Voldemort]] in 1996.`],
 f:[["Category","Non-being"]],
 x:[["ent","The author said Dementors came from her experience of depression."],["ent","According to her, they do not reproduce: they spring up like fungi, wherever there is decay."],["ent","After the war, [[kingsley|Shacklebolt]] removed them from Azkaban."]]},
bichopapao:{t:"criatura",g:"Non-beings and spirits",c:"trevas",n:"Boggart",s:"Whatever frightens the onlooker most",
 p:[`It lives in dark, closed-in places, such as wardrobes and drawers, and nobody knows what shape it has when it is alone. Faced with someone, it becomes that person's greatest fear. The counter-charm is Riddikulus: forcing it to take a funny shape and laughing.`,
 `[[rony|Ron]]'s is a giant spider. [[lupin|Lupin]]'s, the full moon. [[harry|Harry]]'s, a [[dementadores|Dementor]]. Molly [[weasley|Weasley]]'s, the bodies of her family.`],
 f:[["Category","Non-being"]],
 x:[["ent","Dumbledore's would be the corpse of his sister, Ariana. Voldemort's, his own corpse."]]},
fantasmas:{t:"criatura",g:"Non-beings and spirits",c:"pedra",n:"Ghosts",s:"The imprint of wizards who did not move on",
 p:[`Only wizards can become ghosts, and only those who feared death or did not want to depart. They are transparent, pass through walls, do not eat, and walking through one is icy. Each [[hogwarts|Hogwarts]] house has its own: Nearly Headless Nick, the Bloody Baron, the Grey Lady and the Fat Friar.`,
 `There is also Professor Binns, of History of Magic, who died in his sleep and went to teach the next day, and Moaning Myrtle, a student killed by the [[basilisco|basilisk]] in 1943, who haunts the bathroom where the entrance to the [[camara|Chamber of Secrets]] lies.`,
 `Peeves is not a ghost. He is a poltergeist, a spirit of chaos that was never a person, and obeys only the Bloody Baron.`],
 f:[["Category","Spirit"]],
 x:[["site","Ghosts stay tied to the places where they lived. The author describes Peeves as something that came into being with the castle and that no caretaker has ever managed to drive out."]]},
inferi:{t:"criatura",g:"Non-beings and spirits",c:"trevas",n:"Inferi",s:"Corpses animated by dark magic",
 p:[`Bodies bewitched to obey a dark wizard. They have neither will nor soul, feel no pain, and fear fire and light. [[voldemort|Voldemort]] killed enough people to build an army of them and filled with Inferi the lake of the cave where he hid the locket.`,
 `They are neither ghosts nor the dead brought back to life. No magic can resurrect the dead.`],
 f:[["Category","Non-being"]]},

/* ---------- BEASTS ---------- */
dragoes:{t:"criatura",g:"XXXXX beasts",c:"grif",n:"Dragons",s:"Ten pure breeds",
 p:[`The most famous beasts and the hardest to hide. Breeding them has been illegal since 1709. Heart, blood, horn, hide and liver all have magical uses, and the heartstring is one of the three [[varinhas|wand]] cores used by Ollivander. [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] discovered the twelve uses of dragon's blood.`,
 `In the story: Norbert, the Norwegian Ridgeback that [[hagrid|Hagrid]] hatched in his hut, and who turned out to be female. The four of the first task of the [[tribruxo|Triwizard Tournament]]. The blind dragon of [[gringotes|Gringotts]], on which the trio escaped.`],
 mom:"XXXXX",
 br:[["Antipodean Opaleye","New Zealand. The most beautiful and the least aggressive."],["Chinese Fireball","China. Breathes mushroom-shaped flames."],["Common Welsh Green","Wales. Avoids humans."],["Hebridean Black","Scotland. Tended for centuries by the MacFusty clan."],["Hungarian Horntail","Hungary. The most dangerous, and Harry's in the tournament."],["Norwegian Ridgeback","Norway. Norbert's breed."],["Peruvian Vipertooth","Peru. The smallest and the fastest."],["Romanian Longhorn","Romania, home of the world's largest reserve."],["Swedish Short-Snout","Sweden. Blue flame."],["Ukrainian Ironbelly","Ukraine. The largest of all."]],bt:"The ten breeds",
 x:[["lt","The list of breeds comes from Fantastic Beasts and Where to Find Them."]]},
basilisco:{t:"criatura",g:"XXXXX beasts",c:"sons",n:"Basilisk",s:"The King of Serpents",
 p:[`A giant serpent hatched from a chicken's egg incubated by a toad. It can live for centuries. Its direct gaze kills instantly. Seen by reflection, it petrifies. Its venom is so strong it destroys [[horcruxes|Horcruxes]]. Only [[fenix|phoenix]] tears cure it. Spiders flee from it, and the crow of a rooster kills it.`,
 `The one in the [[camara|Chamber of Secrets]] was left by [[salazar|Slytherin]] and obeyed the [[ofidioglossia|Parselmouths]] of his line. It killed Myrtle in 1943 and petrified several students in 1992 and 1993, until [[harry|Harry]] killed it with the [[espada|Sword of Gryffindor]].`],
 mom:"XXXXX",
 x:[["lt","The first basilisk was bred by Herpo the Foul, a dark wizard of ancient Greece."]]},
acromantula:{t:"criatura",g:"XXXXX beasts",c:"trevas",n:"Acromantula",s:"The giant spider that talks",
 p:[`An eight-eyed spider with legs up to 15 feet (4.5 m) long, native to Borneo, capable of human speech and carnivorous. It is believed to have been bred by wizards to guard treasure.`,
 `Aragog, raised by [[hagrid|Hagrid]] from the egg, founded a colony in the [[floresta|Forbidden Forest]]. He spared Hagrid out of friendship, and no one else. His descendants fought alongside the [[comensais|Death Eaters]] in the Battle of Hogwarts.`],
 mom:"XXXXX"},
mortalha:{t:"criatura",g:"XXXXX beasts",c:"trevas",n:"Other XXXXX beasts",s:"Lethifold, Nundu, Chimaera, Manticore and Quintaped",
 p:[`The beasts that not even experts face. The Lethifold is a black cloak that glides at night in the tropics and digests its victim in bed. Only the [[patrono|Patronus]] stops it. The Nundu, from East Africa, is a giant leopard whose breath spreads disease, and it has never been subdued by fewer than a hundred wizards.`,
 `The Greek Chimaera has the head of a lion, the body of a goat and the tail of a dragon. The Manticore has a human head, the body of a lion and the tail of a scorpion, and sings while devouring. The Quintaped lives only on the Isle of Drear, in Scotland: five legs, russet hair and a taste for human flesh. Legend says they are a clan of wizards transfigured by a rival clan.`],
 mom:"XXXXX",
 x:[["lt","All described in Fantastic Beasts and Where to Find Them."]]},
fenix:{t:"criatura",g:"XXXX beasts",c:"grif",n:"Phoenix",s:"The bird that is reborn from the ashes",
 p:[`A scarlet and gold bird the size of a swan. When it grows old, it bursts into flame and is reborn from the ashes. Its tears heal, its song gives courage to the pure of heart, and it can carry enormous weights. It is almost impossible to domesticate.`,
 `Fawkes, [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]]'s phoenix, gave the two feathers in the [[varinhas|wands]] of [[harry|Harry]] and [[voldemort|Voldemort]]. He saved Harry in the [[camara|Chamber of Secrets]] and left Hogwarts for good after the headmaster's death.`],
 mom:"XXXX",
 x:[["af","The films tie the phoenix to the Dumbledore family: one appears to any of them in great need."]]},
testralio:{t:"criatura",g:"XXXX beasts",c:"pedra",n:"Thestral",s:"The winged horse only some can see",
 p:[`A skeletal winged horse with black skin and bat's wings. Only those who have seen someone die and understood what they saw can see it. That is why it has a reputation as an ill omen, undeserved: it is gentle and has a perfect sense of direction.`,
 `The [[hogwarts|Hogwarts]] herd pulls the carriages that seem to move on their own. [[harry|Harry]] began to see them after [[cedrico|Cedric]]'s death. The hair of its tail is the core of the [[reliquias|Elder Wand]].`],
 mom:"XXXX"},
unicornio:{t:"criatura",g:"XXXX beasts",c:"pedra",n:"Unicorn",s:"Purity and a curse",
 p:[`A white one-horned horse, golden as a foal. Horn and tail hair are used in potions and [[varinhas|wands]]. The blood keeps alive someone at death's door, but killing something so pure condemns the person to a cursed half-life.`,
 `That is what [[voldemort|Voldemort]] did in the [[floresta|Forbidden Forest]] in 1992, through Quirrell.`],
 mom:"XXXX"},
hipogrifo:{t:"criatura",g:"XXX beasts",c:"pedra",n:"Hippogriff",s:"Half eagle, half horse",
 p:[`The head, wings and forelegs of a giant eagle, the body of a horse. Extremely proud: you must look it in the eye, bow and wait for it to bow back. Whoever insults it gets clawed.`,
 `Draco [[malfoy|Malfoy]] insulted Buckbeak in [[hagrid|Hagrid]]'s first lesson, and the creature was sentenced to death. [[harry|Harry]] and [[hermione|Hermione]] saved him with the [[viratempo|Time-Turner]], and [[sirius|Sirius]] escaped riding him.`],
 mom:"XXX"},
pelucio:{t:"criatura",g:"XXX beasts",c:"lufa",n:"Niffler",s:"The treasure sniffer",
 p:[`A furry black creature with a long snout that lives in burrows and is mad about anything shiny. Goblins use them to dig for treasure. Gentle and affectionate, it can wreck a house in minutes if there is anything glittering inside.`,
 `[[hagrid|Hagrid]] used them in a lesson, and someone let one loose in [[umbridge|Umbridge]]'s office.`],
 mom:"XXX",
 x:[["af","The Niffler in [[newt|Newt Scamander]]'s suitcase is what causes the chaos at the bank in New York, in 1926."]]},
tronquilho:{t:"criatura",g:"XX beasts",c:"lufa",n:"Bowtruckle",s:"The guardian of the trees",
 p:[`It looks like a twig with two little brown eyes and is about a hand-span tall. It lives in trees whose wood is used for [[varinhas|wands]] and defends them by poking the eyes of anyone who comes near. It is soothed with woodlice.`],
 mom:"XX",
 x:[["af","Pickett, the Bowtruckle who lives in [[newt|Newt]]'s pocket, picks locks in the films."]]},
seminviso:{t:"criatura",g:"XXXX beasts",c:"pedra",n:"Demiguise",s:"Where ordinary Invisibility Cloaks come from",
 p:[`It looks like a graceful monkey with long, silvery hair, and turns invisible when it feels threatened. Invisibility cloaks are woven from its hair, and they lose their effect over the years. [[harry|Harry]]'s cloak is not like that: it is one of the [[reliquias|Deathly Hallows]] and never fails.`],
 mom:"XXXX",
 x:[["af","In the films the Demiguise also foresees the immediate future, which makes it almost impossible to capture."]]},
explosivim:{t:"criatura",g:"XXX beasts",c:"pedra",n:"Blast-Ended Skrewts and Hagrid's other inventions",s:"Hagrid's experiments in breeding",
 p:[`An illegal cross between a manticore and a fire crab, made by [[hagrid|Hagrid]] in 1994. It looks like a shell-less lobster, grows up to 10 feet (3 m), burns, stings and sucks, and lets off explosions from its tail end to propel itself. One of them guarded the maze of the [[tribruxo|Triwizard Tournament]].`,
 `Hagrid also bred Fluffy, a three-headed dog that falls asleep to music and guarded the trapdoor to the [[pedrafilosofal|Philosopher's Stone]].`]},
occami:{t:"criatura",g:"XXXX beasts",c:"pedra",n:"Occamy, Erumpent and Thunderbird",s:"The stars of Fantastic Beasts",
 p:[`The Occamy is a winged, feathered serpent from Asia that grows or shrinks to fill the space available. It lays eggs of pure silver. The Erumpent is an African beast resembling a rhinoceros, whose horn injects a fluid that makes whatever it pierces explode. One such horn brought down the Lovegood house.`,
 `The Thunderbird is North American, a relative of the [[fenix|phoenix]], and creates storms when it flies. It gives its name to one of the houses of [[ilvermorny|Ilvermorny]].`],
 mom:"XXXX",
 x:[["af","All three are in [[newt|Newt]]'s suitcase in the first film. The Thunderbird, Frank, is the reason for his trip to the United States."],["lt","The Thunderbird was added to the 2017 edition of the book, along with five other North American beasts."]]},
pomorim:{t:"criatura",g:"XXXX beasts",c:"lufa",n:"Golden Snidget",s:"The bird that became the Snitch",
 p:[`A round golden little bird with a thin beak, able to change direction in mid-flight with absurd agility. It was used in [[quadribol|Quidditch]] from 1269: whoever caught it earned 150 points, in memory of the 150 Galleons offered in the first hunt.`,
 `It was nearly driven to extinction. It became a protected species in the 14th century, and the Golden Snitch was invented to replace it.`],
 mom:"XXXX",
 x:[["lt","The high rating exists to protect it: injuring or capturing a Snidget carries a heavy penalty."]]},
grindylow:{t:"criatura",g:"XX beasts",c:"pedra",n:"Water beasts",s:"Grindylow, kappa, kelpie and the giant squid",
 p:[`The Grindylow is a pale green water demon with horns and long, brittle fingers. It lives in British lakes, including the one at [[hogwarts|Hogwarts]], and was one of the obstacles of the second task of the [[tribruxo|Triwizard Tournament]].`,
 `The kappa is a Japanese demon with a hollow full of water on top of its head. The kelpie is a British and Irish demon that changes shape and usually appears as a horse. The largest kelpie in the world is the Loch Ness monster. The Hogwarts lake also holds a giant squid, gentle, which the students feed with toast.`],
 mom:"XX"},
amasso:{t:"criatura",g:"XXX beasts",c:"pedra",n:"Kneazles and other pets",s:"Kneazle, Crup, Puffskein and owl",
 p:[`The Kneazle looks like a cat with large ears and a lion's tail. It is very intelligent and sniffs out dishonest people. Crookshanks, [[hermione|Hermione]]'s cat, is part Kneazle, and distrusted Scabbers from the first day.`,
 `The Crup is a dog with a forked tail, bred by wizards and fierce with Muggles. The Puffskein is a purring ball of fur. Hogwarts students may bring an owl, a cat or a toad. Owls carry the wizarding post and find the recipient without an address.`],
 mom:"XXX",
 x:[["site","Arabella Figg, Harry's [[sangue|Squib]] neighbour, makes a living crossing cats with Kneazles."]]},
gnomo:{t:"criatura",g:"XX beasts",c:"pedra",n:"Garden and household pests",s:"Gnomes, pixies and doxies",
 p:[`The garden gnome is about a hand-span tall and has a potato-like head. To get rid of one you have to swing it round until it is dizzy and throw it over the fence, and it comes back. Cornish pixies are blue and love mayhem. [[lockhart|Lockhart]] let a cage of them loose in the classroom and could not round them up.`,
 `Doxies have two pairs of arms and venomous teeth, and infested the curtains of [[grimmauld|Grimmauld Place]]. The Flobberworm, rated X, is a brown worm that eats lettuce and does nothing else.`],
 mom:"XX"},
esfinge:{t:"criatura",g:"XXXX beasts",c:"pedra",n:"Sphinx, Griffin and winged horses",s:"The guardians",
 p:[`The Egyptian sphinx has a human head and a lion's body, speaks and lets pass only those who solve its riddle. One of them guarded the maze of the [[tribruxo|Triwizard Tournament]]. The Griffin, with an eagle's head and a lion's body, is also used to guard treasure.`,
 `There are four breeds of winged horse: the Abraxan, a giant palomino that pulls the [[escolas|Beauxbatons]] carriage and drinks only single-malt whisky, the Aethonan, the Granian and the [[testralio|Thestral]].`],
 mom:"XXXX"},
obscurus:{t:"criatura",g:"Magical phenomena",c:"trevas",n:"Obscurus",s:"Repressed magic that comes to life",
 p:[`When a young wizard is forced to hide or hate their own magic, that magic can turn inward and form an Obscurus: a dark, parasitic force that explodes uncontrollably. The child, the Obscurial, rarely lives past ten.`,
 `They were common in the centuries of witch-hunts and became extremely rare after the [[estatuto|Statute of Secrecy]].`],
 f:[["Category","Parasitic magical force"]],
 x:[["af","The concept appears in the first Fantastic Beasts film, with [[credence|Credence Barebone]]."]]},
maledictus:{t:"criatura",g:"Magical phenomena",c:"trevas",n:"Maledictus and Nagini",s:"The blood curse",
 p:[`Nagini is [[voldemort|Voldemort]]'s snake, the last [[horcruxes|Horcrux]] he made, killed by [[neville|Neville]] in the final battle. In the books she is only that: an enormous venomous serpent that he controls.`],
 x:[["af","The second film gave her a past. Nagini was a woman, a Maledictus: the bearer of a blood curse, passed from mother to daughter, that turns her into an animal until the change becomes permanent. In 1927 she worked in a circus in Paris."],["ent","The author stated that she had been keeping this story for about twenty years."]]},
americanas:{t:"criatura",g:"Around the world",c:"pedra",n:"North American creatures",s:"Horned Serpent, Wampus and Pukwudgie",
 p:[`The four houses of [[ilvermorny|Ilvermorny]] are named after local creatures. The Horned Serpent has a jewel on its forehead and powers of divination. The Wampus is a fast feline, almost impossible to kill, whose hair goes into American [[varinhas|wands]]. The Thunderbird creates storms.`,
 `The Pukwudgie is a distant relative of the European goblin: short, with a grey face and big ears, independent, with magic of its own and poisoned arrows.`],
 x:[["site","They come from the author's 2016 texts on Ilvermorny and on magic in North America."]]},
caipora:{t:"criatura",g:"Around the world",c:"sons",n:"Caipora",s:"The guardians of Castelobruxo",
 p:[`Small, furry forest spirits, mischievous and cunning, who come out at night to watch over the students and creatures of [[castelobruxo|Castelobruxo]], the school of magic in Brazil.`],
 x:[["site","They appear in the author's text on Castelobruxo. She tells how a former headmistress, on an exchange visit, laughed when the Hogwarts headmaster complained about Peeves and offered to send some Caiporas to the Forbidden Forest, to show him what real trouble is. The offer was declined."]]},
qilin:{t:"criatura",g:"Around the world",c:"pedra",n:"Qilin and Zouwu",s:"The Chinese creatures of the films",
 p:[`The Qilin is a rare creature, resembling a scaly deer, which sees into people's souls and bows before those who are pure of heart. It was used to choose the leaders of the wizarding world. The Zouwu is a feline the size of an elephant, with a long, colourful tail, which covers a thousand miles in a day.`],
 x:[["af","The Zouwu appears in the second film. The Qilin is at the centre of the third: [[grindelwald|Grindelwald]] kills one and reanimates it to rig the election of the [[confederacao|International Confederation]]."]]},
});
Object.assign(E, {
/* ---------- MAGIC ---------- */
varinhas:{t:"magia",g:"Fundamentals",c:"magia",n:"Wands",s:"The wand chooses the wizard",
 p:[`Almost all European magic goes through a wand: a piece of wood with a core taken from a magical creature. Wood, core, length and flexibility give each one a temperament. No two are alike, and it is the wand that chooses its owner.`,
 `Loyalty can change. A wand truly won, by disarming or defeating its former owner, comes to serve the winner better. It is the rule that decides the war: the Elder Wand changed masters when Draco [[malfoy|Malfoy]] disarmed [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]], and again when [[harry|Harry]] took Draco's wand.`,
 `Two wands with cores from the same creature are twins and refuse to fight each other. Forced to duel, they produce Priori Incantatem: one makes the other repeat, in reverse, the last spells it cast. It happened between Harry and [[voldemort|Voldemort]] in the graveyard, in 1995.`],
 br:[["Phoenix feather","The rarest core. Capable of the greatest range of magic, acts on its own initiative and is slow to accept an owner."],["Dragon heartstring","The most powerful and the quickest to learn. Temperamental, the most prone to accidents."],["Unicorn hair","The most faithful and constant, and the hardest to turn to the Dark Arts."]],bt:"Ollivander's three cores",
 f:[["Harry","Holly and phoenix feather, 11 inches (28 cm)"],["Voldemort","Yew and phoenix feather, 13½ inches (34 cm)"],["Hermione","Vine wood and dragon heartstring"],["Draco","Hawthorn and unicorn hair"],["The Elder Wand","Elder and Thestral tail hair"]],
 x:[["site","The [[olivaras|Ollivanders]] have made wands since 382 BC. The texts about woods and cores are presented as notes by Garrick Ollivander."],["site","Outside Europe other cores are used: Wampus hair, Thunderbird tail feather and Horned Serpent horn in the United States. At Uagadou, in Africa, many wizards do without a wand and do magic with gestures."],["ent","The author gave Harry, Ron and Hermione woods from the Celtic tree calendar matching their birthdays."]]},
feiticos:{t:"magia",g:"Fundamentals",c:"magia",n:"Spells",s:"Charms, hexes and curses",
 p:[`Wand magic requires three things: the movement, the word and the intention. Experienced wizards can do without the word and cast non-verbal spells, taught in sixth year. Children do magic by accident when they are frightened or angry, before any lesson.`,
 `The books distinguish types. Transfiguration changes what a thing is. A Charm adds a property to what it already is. Hexes, jinxes and curses are attacking magic, in rising order of wickedness. There are also counter-spells and healing magic.`,
 `Magic has limits. You cannot create food out of nothing, nor money, and you cannot bring anyone back from the dead.`],
 br:[["Expelliarmus","Disarms. Harry's trademark, and the spell with which he defeats Voldemort."],["Expecto Patronum","Conjures the [[patrono|Patronus]]."],["Stupefy","Stuns: leaves the target unconscious."],["Protego","A shield that deflects spells."],["Accio","Summons an object to the caller."],["Wingardium Leviosa","Makes things levitate. The first spell the class learns."],["Alohomora","Unlocks."],["Lumos and Nox","Light and extinguish the tip of the wand."],["Petrificus Totalus","Paralyses the whole body."],["Obliviate","Erases memories. Used every day by the Ministry on Muggles who saw too much."],["Riddikulus","Defeats the Boggart."],["Reparo","Mends what is broken."],["Sectumsempra","Cuts like a sword. Snape's invention."],["Fiendfyre","Cursed fire that chases its victim. One of the few things that destroy Horcruxes."]],bt:"The most seen in the story"},
imperdoaveis:{t:"magia",g:"Dark Arts",c:"trevas",n:"Unforgivable Curses",s:"Imperius, Cruciatus and the Killing Curse",
 p:[`Three curses whose use on another human being earns life imprisonment in [[azkaban|Azkaban]]. They were classified as such in 1717.`,
 `During the first war, Barty [[crouch|Crouch]] authorised the [[aurores|Aurors]] to use them. When [[voldemort|Voldemort]] took over the Ministry, in 1997, the ban fell, and they came to be taught at Hogwarts by the Carrows.`],
 br:[["Imperio, the Imperius Curse","Total control over another's will. It can be resisted, with great effort. After the first war, many Death Eaters claimed to have acted under it."],["Crucio, the Cruciatus Curse","Unbearable pain. For it to work, you must mean to cause the pain and enjoy it."],["Avada Kedavra, the Killing Curse","A flash of green light, instant death and no mark. It has no counter-curse and no shield. Only Harry has survived it, twice."]],bt:"The three"},
trevas:{t:"magia",g:"Dark Arts",c:"trevas",n:"The Dark Arts",s:"Magic made to hurt, dominate and kill",
 p:[`It is not a separate branch of magic, but the use of it to cause harm. It ranges from corridor hexes to the [[imperdoaveis|Unforgivable Curses]], the [[inferi|Inferi]] and the [[horcruxes|Horcruxes]]. The Dark Mark, a skull with a snake coming out of its mouth, is conjured by the [[comensais|Death Eaters]] over the places where they have killed.`,
 `Hogwarts teaches how to defend against it. [[escolas|Durmstrang]] actually teaches it. The post of Defence Against the Dark Arts professor was cursed by [[voldemort|Voldemort]] when [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] denied him the job: since then no one has lasted more than a year.`],
 br:[["1991","Quirinus Quirrell, with Voldemort on the back of his head."],["1992","Gilderoy Lockhart."],["1993","Remus Lupin."],["1994","Barty Crouch Jr., disguised as Alastor Moody."],["1995","Dolores Umbridge."],["1996","Severus Snape."],["1997","Amycus Carrow, who taught the Dark Arts without the 'Defence'."]],bt:"Harry's seven professors",
 x:[["ent","The curse on the post ended with Voldemort's death."]]},
horcruxes:{t:"magia",g:"Dark Arts",c:"trevas",n:"Horcruxes",s:"Pieces of soul hidden in objects",
 p:[`A Horcrux is an object that holds a piece of a wizard's soul. As long as it exists, the wizard cannot truly die, even if his body is destroyed. To split the soul you must commit the worst of acts: murder.`,
 `No one before [[voldemort|Voldemort]] had made more than one. He wanted his soul in seven parts, the most powerful magical number: six Horcruxes and the piece in his own body. He made one more without knowing. When the curse rebounded on him in 1981, a fragment of soul, already unstable, clung to the only living thing in the room.`,
 `Only very destructive magic destroys a Horcrux: [[basilisco|basilisk]] venom, Fiendfyre or the [[espada|Sword of Gryffindor]] once imbued with the venom.`],
 br:[["Tom Riddle's diary","Made with the death of Myrtle, in 1943. Destroyed by Harry with a basilisk fang, in 1993."],["The Gaunt ring","Made with the death of his father. It held the Resurrection Stone. Destroyed by Dumbledore with the sword, in 1996."],["Slytherin's locket","Hidden in the cave, swapped by Regulus Black. Destroyed by Ron with the sword."],["Hufflepuff's cup","Kept in the Lestranges' vault at Gringotts. Destroyed by Hermione with a basilisk fang."],["Ravenclaw's diadem","Hidden in the Room of Requirement. Destroyed by Fiendfyre cast by Crabbe."],["Harry Potter","The accidental Horcrux. The fragment was destroyed by Voldemort's Killing Curse in the Forbidden Forest."],["Nagini","The snake. Killed by Neville with the sword."]],bt:"The seven, in order of creation",
 x:[["ent","The author completed the list of murders used: the locket was made with that of a Muggle tramp, the cup with that of Hepzibah Smith, the diadem with that of an Albanian peasant and Nagini with that of Bertha Jorkins."],["lt","The first known Horcrux is attributed to Herpo the Foul, the same Greek wizard who bred the first basilisk."]]},
reliquias:{t:"magia",g:"Legendary objects",c:"magia",n:"Deathly Hallows",s:"The wand, the stone and the cloak",
 p:[`Three objects which, according to the Tale of the Three Brothers, in Beedle the Bard, were given by Death to the [[peverell|Peverell]] brothers. Whoever united all three would be the Master of Death. The symbol is a triangle, a circle and a line. [[grindelwald|Grindelwald]] adopted it, which is why many people take it for a mark of the Dark.`,
 `[[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] and Grindelwald sought them in their youth. Dumbledore came to hold all three, at different times. [[harry|Harry]] was the only one to possess them at the same time, and to understand the title another way: the master of death is the one who accepts dying.`],
 br:[["The Elder Wand","The most powerful in existence, made of elder. It passes to whoever defeats its previous owner, and has left a trail of murders. From Gregorovitch to Grindelwald, to Dumbledore, to Draco Malfoy, to Harry. Harry used it to repair his own wand and returned it to Dumbledore's tomb."],["The Resurrection Stone","It does not resurrect anyone. It brings shadows of the dead, which only the holder can see. It was in the Gaunt ring. Harry used it to walk to Voldemort and let it fall in the Forbidden Forest."],["The Cloak of Invisibility","The only one that neither wears out nor fails. It passed from Ignotus Peverell to the Potters, from father to son."]],bt:"The three Hallows",
 x:[["lt","The Tales of Beedle the Bard contains the full tale, with commentary by Dumbledore."]]},
patrono:{t:"magia",g:"Fundamentals",c:"magia",n:"Patronus",s:"Expecto Patronum",
 p:[`A guardian made of pure happiness, which the [[dementadores|Dementor]] cannot drain because it feels no despair. It is advanced magic, beyond O.W.L. level. It demands concentrating on the happiest memory the person has while the Dementor empties them.`,
 `A full Patronus has the form of an animal, unique to each wizard, and can change after a deep shock: [[tonks|Tonks]]'s changed when she fell in love. The [[ordem|Order of the Phoenix]] uses Patronuses to send messages, an invention of [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]]'s.`],
 br:[["Harry","Stag, his father's Animagus form."],["Lily and Snape","Doe."],["Hermione","Otter."],["Ron","Jack Russell terrier."],["Dumbledore","Phoenix."],["McGonagall","Cat."],["Kingsley Shacklebolt","Lynx."],["Arthur Weasley","Weasel."],["Luna","Hare."],["Umbridge","Cat."]],bt:"Some Patronuses",
 x:[["site","Most wizards never manage a corporeal Patronus. Dark wizards rarely try: the spell can turn against anyone unworthy of it."]]},
animagos:{t:"magia",g:"Gifts and techniques",c:"magia",n:"Animagi",s:"Wizards who turn into animals",
 p:[`An Animagus turns into a specific animal at will, keeping a human mind. The form is not chosen. The process is long and dangerous, and the [[ministerio|Ministry]] requires registration: in the 20th century there were seven registered, [[mcgonagall|McGonagall]] among them.`,
 `The unregistered ones matter more in the story: [[tiagolilian|James Potter]] (stag), [[sirius|Sirius Black]] (dog), [[pettigrew|Peter Pettigrew]] (rat) and [[skeeter|Rita Skeeter]] (beetle). It was as a dog that Sirius resisted the Dementors and escaped from Azkaban.`],
 x:[["site","The ritual involves keeping a mandrake leaf in the mouth for a whole month, from full moon to full moon, and waiting for a thunderstorm."]]},
metamorfomagos:{t:"magia",g:"Gifts and techniques",c:"magia",n:"Metamorphmagi",s:"Changing appearance at will",
 p:[`A very rare gift, from birth, that cannot be learned. A Metamorphmagus changes hair, face and body without wand or potion. [[tonks|Tonks]] is one, and her son, Teddy Lupin, inherited the gift.`]},
legilimencia:{t:"magia",g:"Gifts and techniques",c:"magia",n:"Legilimency and Occlumency",s:"Entering the mind and closing the mind",
 p:[`Legilimency is the art of extracting feelings and memories from another person's mind. It is not reading thoughts like a book. [[voldemort|Voldemort]] and [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] were masters, and it is almost impossible to lie to a Legilimens.`,
 `Occlumency is the defence: emptying the mind and hiding what one feels. [[snape|Snape]] fooled Voldemort for years thanks to it and tried, unsuccessfully, to teach it to [[harry|Harry]] in 1996.`],
 x:[["af","Queenie Goldstein, in the films, is a natural Legilimens, who hears the thoughts of anyone nearby without effort."]]},
ofidioglossia:{t:"magia",g:"Gifts and techniques",c:"sons",n:"Parseltongue",s:"The language of snakes",
 p:[`The ability to speak with snakes. It is hereditary, extremely rare and associated with the Dark Arts, being the mark of [[salazar|Salazar Slytherin]] and his descendants, [[gaunt|the Gaunts]]. The entrance to the [[camara|Chamber of Secrets]] opens only for someone who speaks it.`,
 `[[harry|Harry]] spoke it because of the piece of [[voldemort|Voldemort]]'s soul he carried. [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] understood it. [[rony|Ron]] opened the Chamber in 1998 by imitating the sound he had heard Harry make.`]},
transporte:{t:"magia",g:"Magical life",c:"magia",n:"Magical transport",s:"Apparition, Floo powder, Portkeys and brooms",
 p:[`To Apparate is to vanish from one place and appear in another. It requires a licence, taken at seventeen, and whoever gets it wrong may be splinched, leaving part of the body behind. You cannot Apparate inside [[hogwarts|Hogwarts]].`,
 `The Floo Network links wizarding fireplaces: you throw the powder into the fire, step into the green flames and say your destination clearly. A Portkey is any object enchanted to carry whoever touches it to a set place at a set time.`,
 `Brooms are personal transport and the equipment of [[quadribol|Quidditch]]. Flying carpets are banned in Britain. The Knight Bus picks up stranded wizards, and the Hogwarts Express leaves from platform 9¾ at King's Cross station every 1 September at eleven in the morning.`],
 x:[["site","The Express was the idea of Minister Ottaline Gambol, who governed from 1827 to 1835: a Muggle locomotive, obtained in an operation with many Memory Charms. Before it, each family took their children as best they could."],["site","Floo powder was invented by Ignatia Wildsmith in the 13th century."]]},
profecia:{t:"magia",g:"Gifts and techniques",c:"magia",n:"Prophecies and seers",s:"The prophecy that drives the story",
 p:[`Divination is the vaguest subject at Hogwarts, and true seers are rare. A genuine prophecy is spoken in a trance, and the speaker does not remember it. The [[misterios|Department of Mysteries]] keeps a record of each one, in glass spheres that only the people named can pick up.`,
 `In 1980, [[trelawney|Sybill Trelawney]] predicted in front of [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] that there would be born, at the end of July, to parents who had thrice defied the Dark Lord, the one with the power to vanquish him. The Dark Lord would mark him as his equal, and one would have to die at the hand of the other.`,
 `[[snape|Snape]] heard only the first half and carried it to [[voldemort|Voldemort]]. There were two possible boys, [[harry|Harry]] and [[neville|Neville]]. By attacking Harry, Voldemort chose and himself fulfilled the part about marking him. Dumbledore insists on this: the prophecy only mattered because Voldemort believed it.`]},
viratempo:{t:"magia",g:"Magical objects",c:"magia",n:"Time-Turner",s:"An hourglass that turns back the hours",
 p:[`A small hourglass on a chain. Each turn sends the wearer back one hour. Its use is controlled by the [[ministerio|Ministry]], and the main rule is not to be seen by yourself. [[hermione|Hermione]] was given one in 1993 to attend classes at the same time, and with it she saved [[sirius|Sirius]] and Buckbeak.`,
 `The Ministry's entire stock was destroyed in the battle of the [[misterios|Department of Mysteries]], in 1996.`],
 x:[["site","According to the author, the safe limit is five hours. Longer journeys caused disasters, and that is why Time-Turners carry a spell that stops them going further."],["peca","The play features an illegal Time-Turner, able to go back years, and shows the alternative timelines it creates."]]},
penseira:{t:"magia",g:"Magical objects",c:"magia",n:"Pensieve",s:"A basin for reviewing memories",
 p:[`A stone basin engraved with runes, into which memories drawn from the head with a wand are poured, as silvery strands. Whoever dips their face in it enters the scene and watches it from outside, with everything the person witnessed, whether they noticed it or not.`,
 `It is how [[harry|Harry]] learns [[voldemort|Voldemort]]'s past in his lessons with [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]], and how he discovers the truth about [[snape|Snape]].`],
 x:[["site","The Hogwarts Pensieve is older than the school: the founders are said to have found it half-buried on the spot where they decided to build the castle."]]},
ojesed:{t:"magia",g:"Magical objects",c:"magia",n:"Mirror of Erised",s:"The deepest desire",
 p:[`A mirror that shows the deepest, most desperate desire of the heart of whoever looks into it. 'Erised' is 'desire' spelled backwards. [[harry|Harry]] saw himself with his parents and family. [[rony|Ron]] saw himself as Head Boy and Quidditch captain.`,
 `[[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] used it as the last protection of the [[pedrafilosofal|Philosopher's Stone]]: only someone who wanted to find it without wanting to use it would see it in the mirror.`]},
pedrafilosofal:{t:"magia",g:"Legendary objects",c:"magia",n:"Philosopher's Stone",s:"Gold and endless life",
 p:[`The supreme work of alchemy: it turns any metal into pure gold and produces the Elixir of Life, which keeps death at bay for as long as it is drunk. The only one known was made by [[flamel|Nicolas Flamel]].`,
 `In 1991 it was taken from [[gringotes|Gringotts]] to Hogwarts and guarded by seven protections, one from each teacher. [[voldemort|Voldemort]], in Quirrell's body, tried to steal it in order to return. It was destroyed in 1992.`]},
chapeu:{t:"magia",g:"Hogwarts objects",c:"magia",n:"Sorting Hat",s:"Who decides each student's house",
 p:[`A patched wizard's hat that belonged to [[godrico|Godric Gryffindor]]. The four founders gave it intelligence so that it would go on sorting students into houses after them. Every 1 September it sings a new song and is placed on the head of each first-year.`,
 `It sees what a person is and also takes into account what they choose. It wanted to put [[harry|Harry]] in [[sonserina|Slytherin]] and granted his request. Twice it handed the [[espada|Sword of Gryffindor]] to someone who needed it: to Harry in the [[camara|Chamber of Secrets]] and to [[neville|Neville]] in the final battle.`],
 x:[["site","A Sorting that takes more than five minutes is a 'Hatstall', and happens about once every fifty years."]]},
espada:{t:"magia",g:"Hogwarts objects",c:"grif",n:"Sword of Gryffindor",s:"Goblin-made silver, ruby-studded hilt",
 p:[`The sword of [[godrico|Godric Gryffindor]], made by [[duendes|goblins]]. Their silver absorbs whatever strengthens it, and after killing the [[basilisco|basilisk]] the blade became imbued with the venom. It thus became one of the few weapons able to destroy [[horcruxes|Horcruxes]].`,
 `It presents itself to any [[grifinoria|Gryffindor]] student worthy of it, in real need. It destroyed the ring, the locket and Nagini.`]},
mapa:{t:"magia",g:"Hogwarts objects",c:"grif",n:"Marauder's Map",s:"I solemnly swear that I am up to no good",
 p:[`A parchment created by the [[marotos|Marauders]] that shows the whole of [[hogwarts|Hogwarts]], with its seven secret passages and a little named dot for every person in the castle. It is not fooled by an Invisibility Cloak, an Animagus or Polyjuice Potion: that is how [[lupin|Lupin]] saw [[pettigrew|Pettigrew]] alive.`,
 `Confiscated by Filch, stolen by Fred and George [[weasley|Weasley]] and given to [[harry|Harry]] in 1993. The Room of Requirement does not appear on it.`]},
fidelius:{t:"magia",g:"Gifts and techniques",c:"magia",n:"Fidelius Charm and Unbreakable Vow",s:"Secrets and oaths",
 p:[`The Fidelius Charm hides a secret inside a person, the Secret-Keeper. No one else can find what was hidden, even looking straight at the place, unless the Secret-Keeper tells them of their own free will. It protected the Potters' house, and [[pettigrew|Pettigrew]] was the Secret-Keeper. It also protects the [[ordem|Order]]'s headquarters at [[grimmauld|Grimmauld Place]].`,
 `The Unbreakable Vow is an oath sealed by a third party with a wand. Whoever breaks it dies. [[snape|Snape]] made one to Narcissa [[malfoy|Malfoy]]: to protect Draco and finish his task if the boy failed.`]},
amor:{t:"magia",g:"Fundamentals",c:"grif",n:"The magic of sacrifice",s:"Lily's protection",
 p:[`The oldest magic in history, and the one [[voldemort|Voldemort]] always despised. When someone chooses to die for another person, when they could save themselves, they leave on that person a protection no curse can pass through. [[tiagolilian|Lily]] had the choice, and that is why the Killing Curse rebounded on whoever cast it.`,
 `[[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] extended the protection by leaving [[harry|Harry]] with Lily's sister: as long as he lived where his mother's blood runs, he would be safe. Voldemort used Harry's blood to rebuild his body, thinking he was stealing the protection. In fact he kept it alive inside himself, and that is what tied Harry to life in the Forbidden Forest.`,
 `In the final battle Harry repeats his mother's act for everyone in the castle, and Voldemort's spells stop taking hold of them.`],
 x:[["ent","The locked room in the Department of Mysteries, which Dumbledore mentions, holds the study of love."]]},
pocoes:{t:"magia",g:"Fundamentals",c:"magia",n:"Potions",s:"The exact science of magic",
 p:[`Potions demands precision rather than a wand: ingredients, order, timing and number of stirs. A bezoar, a stone taken from the stomach of a goat, serves as an antidote to most poisons.`],
 br:[["Polyjuice Potion","Gives the appearance of another person for an hour. Takes a month to brew and needs a piece of whoever you want to imitate. Does not work for turning into an animal."],["Veritaserum","Truth serum, colourless and odourless. Three drops are enough."],["Felix Felicis","Liquid luck, golden. Six months to brew. Banned in competitions."],["Amortentia","The strongest love potion. It creates obsession, not love. The smell is different for each person."],["Wolfsbane Potion","Keeps the werewolf's mind during the transformation."],["Draught of Living Death","A sleep so deep it looks like death."],["Skele-Gro","Makes bones grow back, painfully."],["Elixir of Life","Made with the Philosopher's Stone. Prolongs life for as long as it is drunk."]],bt:"The main ones"},
rastreador:{t:"magia",g:"Magical life",c:"magia",n:"The Trace",s:"The magic of underage wizards",
 p:[`Wizards come of age at seventeen. Before that they carry the Trace, a spell that alerts the [[ministerio|Ministry]] to any magic done near them outside school. The decree banning underage magic dates from 1875.`,
 `The Trace indicates the place, not who cast the spell. That is why [[harry|Harry]] took the blame for [[dobby|Dobby]]'s spell in 1992. In wizarding family homes the Ministry trusts the parents.`]},
materias:{t:"magia",g:"Magical life",c:"magia",n:"The subjects at Hogwarts",s:"What you study in seven years",
 p:[`From first to fifth year everyone takes seven subjects. In third year the student chooses at least two electives. In fifth year they sit the O.W.L.s (Ordinary Wizarding Levels), and the grades decide what they may continue. In seventh year they sit the N.E.W.T.s (Nastily Exhausting Wizarding Tests), required for careers such as [[aurores|Auror]].`,
 `In first year there are flying lessons on broomsticks, and in sixth year, the Apparition course. Each house has two prefects per year from fifth year onwards, and the school has a Head Boy and a Head Girl. The passing grades are Outstanding, Exceeds Expectations and Acceptable. The failing ones: Poor, Dreadful and Troll.`],
 br:[["Transfiguration","Changing the shape and nature of things. The hardest and most exact."],["Charms","Enchantments: giving new properties to what already exists."],["Potions","Brewing potions, in the dungeons."],["Herbology","Magical plants and fungi, in the greenhouses."],["Defence Against the Dark Arts","Dangerous creatures, curses and how to face them."],["Astronomy","At midnight, at the top of the tallest tower."],["History of Magic","Taught by a ghost. Everyone sleeps."],["Electives","Care of Magical Creatures, Divination, Arithmancy, Ancient Runes and Muggle Studies."]],bt:"The subjects",
 x:[["site","Alchemy is offered in sixth and seventh year, when there are enough students."]]},
});
Object.assign(E, {
/* ---------- PLACES ---------- */
hogwarts:{t:"lugar",g:"Hogwarts",c:"magia",n:"Hogwarts",s:"School of Witchcraft and Wizardry",
 p:[`A castle in the Scottish Highlands, on the edge of a lake, founded around 990 by [[godrico|Godric Gryffindor]], [[helga|Helga Hufflepuff]], [[rowena|Rowena Ravenclaw]] and [[salazar|Salazar Slytherin]]. It takes young wizards from Britain and Ireland from the ages of eleven to seventeen, divided into four houses: [[grifinoria|Gryffindor]], [[lufalufa|Hufflepuff]], [[corvinal|Ravenclaw]] and [[sonserina|Slytherin]].`,
 `It has seven floors, 142 staircases that move, portraits that talk and a Great Hall whose ceiling shows the sky outside. To Muggles it looks like a ruin with a danger sign. You cannot Apparate on the grounds, and electrical devices do not work there.`,
 `Every wizarding child born in the country is registered at birth: the admission letter arrives in the year the child turns eleven. The houses compete for points all year, counted in four hourglasses of precious stones, and the one with the most takes the House Cup.`,
 `It was the setting of the final battle, on 2 May 1998.`],
 f:[["Motto","Draco dormiens nunquam titillandus: never tickle a sleeping dragon"],["Founded","Around 990"],["Headmasters in the story","Armando Dippet, Albus Dumbledore, Dolores Umbridge (1996), Severus Snape (1997), Minerva McGonagall"]],
 x:[["site","The name of every wizarding child is written by an enchanted quill in a book kept in a locked tower. The Quill of Acceptance and the Book of Admittance have existed since the founding, and the book sometimes closes against someone the quill wants to enrol."],["site","According to the author's text, Hogwarts' first sanitation came only in the 18th century, and it was the plumbing renovation that nearly revealed the Chamber of Secrets."]]},
camara:{t:"lugar",g:"Hogwarts",c:"sons",n:"Chamber of Secrets",s:"Slytherin's hiding place",
 p:[`A chamber built by [[salazar|Salazar Slytherin]] deep in the castle, before he left the school. The entrance is in a girls' bathroom on the second floor and opens only for someone who speaks the [[ofidioglossia|language of snakes]]. Inside lived the [[basilisco|basilisk]].`,
 `It was opened twice. In 1943 by Tom Riddle, when Myrtle died and [[hagrid|Hagrid]] took the blame. In 1992 by [[gina|Ginny Weasley]], possessed by Riddle's diary. In 1998 [[rony|Ron]] and [[hermione|Hermione]] went back there to collect basilisk fangs.`]},
salaprecisa:{t:"lugar",g:"Hogwarts",c:"magia",n:"Room of Requirement",s:"The room that comes and goes",
 p:[`It is on the seventh floor and appears only to someone who walks past the wall three times thinking about what they need. It becomes whatever the person requires. It was the headquarters of [[armada|Dumbledore's Army]], Draco [[malfoy|Malfoy]]'s workshop and a refuge for persecuted students in 1997.`,
 `In the form of a store for hidden objects, it kept [[horcruxes|Ravenclaw's diadem]] for decades. That version of the room was consumed by Fiendfyre.`]},
floresta:{t:"lugar",g:"Hogwarts",c:"magia",n:"Forbidden Forest",s:"The woodland on the castle grounds",
 p:[`An ancient forest on the edge of the grounds, forbidden to students. [[centauros|Centaurs]], [[unicornio|Unicorns]], [[testralio|Thestrals]], Aragog's colony of [[acromantula|Acromantulas]] and, for a time, the giant Grawp live in it.`,
 `It was there that [[harry|Harry]] saw [[voldemort|Voldemort]] drink unicorn blood in 1992, and where he walked to die in 1998.`]},
hogsmeade:{t:"lugar",g:"Hogwarts",c:"magia",n:"Hogsmeade",s:"Britain's only entirely wizarding village",
 p:[`A village next to [[hogwarts|Hogwarts]], where the Express stops. Students from third year on may visit on certain weekends, with a signed permission slip.`,
 `There you find the Three Broomsticks, with Madam Rosmerta's butterbeer, Honeydukes, Zonko's Joke Shop, [[aberforth|Aberforth]]'s Hog's Head and the [[gritos|Shrieking Shack]].`],
 x:[["site","It was founded by Hengist of Woodcroft, fleeing Muggle persecutors, at about the same time as the school."]]},
gritos:{t:"lugar",g:"Hogwarts",c:"magia",n:"Shrieking Shack",s:"The most haunted house in Britain, which never was",
 p:[`A hovel in [[hogsmeade|Hogsmeade]] linked to Hogwarts by a tunnel under the Whomping Willow. It was prepared so that [[lupin|Remus Lupin]] could transform away from his schoolmates. The howls the villagers heard were his, and [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] encouraged the rumour of ghosts.`,
 `There [[harry|Harry]] learned the truth about [[sirius|Sirius]] and [[pettigrew|Pettigrew]] in 1994, and there [[snape|Snape]] died.`]},
beco:{t:"lugar",g:"London",c:"magia",n:"Diagon Alley",s:"The wizards' shopping street",
 p:[`A street in London hidden behind the Leaky Cauldron, a pub that Muggles do not notice. You get in by tapping the right brick of the back wall with a wand. This is where school supplies are bought: wands at [[olivaras|Ollivanders]], books at Flourish and Blotts, robes at Madam Malkin's, owls at the Eeylops Owl Emporium.`,
 `At the end of the street stands [[gringotes|Gringotts]]. Beside it, Knockturn Alley, devoted to the Dark Arts, where Borgin and Burkes is, the shop where Tom Riddle worked after school. In 1996 the [[weasley|Weasley]] twins opened Weasleys' Wizard Wheezes there.`]},
gringotes:{t:"lugar",g:"London",c:"magia",n:"Gringotts",s:"The wizards' bank",
 p:[`The only wizarding bank in Britain, run by [[duendes|goblins]]. It is a white building in [[beco|Diagon Alley]] above miles of tunnels, with vaults that only goblins can open, dragons on the deepest levels and a waterfall that undoes any magical disguise.`,
 `It was said that only a madman would try to rob it. Quirrell tried in 1991 and found the vault empty. In 1998 [[harry|Harry]], [[rony|Ron]] and [[hermione|Hermione]] broke into the Lestranges' vault, took Hufflepuff's cup and escaped on the dragon.`],
 f:[["Currency","1 gold Galleon = 17 silver Sickles. 1 Sickle = 29 bronze Knuts"]],
 x:[["site","It was founded in 1474 by a goblin called Gringott."]]},
minsede:{t:"lugar",g:"London",c:"magia",n:"Ministry headquarters",s:"Ten floors beneath London",
 p:[`The [[ministerio|Ministry of Magic]] is underground in the centre of London. Visitors enter through a broken telephone box, and staff through the fireplaces in the Atrium. On level nine is the [[misterios|Department of Mysteries]], and on level ten, the old courtrooms.`,
 `The Atrium had the Fountain of Magical Brethren, destroyed in the duel between [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] and [[voldemort|Voldemort]] in 1996. Under Voldemort's regime it was replaced by a statue of wizards seated on Muggles.`]},
misterios:{t:"lugar",g:"London",c:"magia",n:"Department of Mysteries",s:"Where the Unspeakables study what cannot be explained",
 p:[`The most secret section of the [[ministerio|Ministry]]. Its employees, the Unspeakables, may not talk about their work. The rooms study the great enigmas: time, thought, space, death and love. Here are the Hall of Prophecy and the chamber with the archway and the veil, behind which voices can be heard.`,
 `In June 1996 [[voldemort|Voldemort]] lured [[harry|Harry]] there to take the [[profecia|prophecy]]. [[armada|The Army]] and [[ordem|the Order]] fought the [[comensais|Death Eaters]], the prophecy was broken, [[sirius|Sirius]] fell through the veil, and the wizarding world saw that Voldemort had returned.`]},
mungus:{t:"lugar",g:"London",c:"magia",n:"St Mungo's",s:"Hospital for Magical Maladies and Injuries",
 p:[`A wizarding hospital in London, hidden behind the front of a department store closed for refurbishment. The Healers wear lime green. The floors are divided by type of damage: artefact accidents, creature-induced injuries, magical bugs, potion and plant poisoning and spell damage.`,
 `In the permanent spell damage ward live [[neville|Neville]]'s parents and [[lockhart|Gilderoy Lockhart]].`],
 x:[["site","Founded in the 17th century by the Healer Mungo Bonham."]]},
grimmauld:{t:"lugar",g:"London",c:"magia",n:"12 Grimmauld Place",s:"The Black family home, headquarters of the Order",
 p:[`Home of the Most Ancient and Noble House of Black, invisible to the Muggle neighbours, who think it natural that the street jumps from number 11 to 13. It has house-elf heads on the wall, the portrait of [[sirius|Sirius]]'s mother screaming insults and a tapestry with the family tree, from which the disowned were burned away.`,
 `Sirius lent it to the [[ordem|Order of the Phoenix]] in 1995 and left it to [[harry|Harry]]. The trio hid there in 1997.`]},
toca:{t:"lugar",g:"Homes",c:"grif",n:"The Burrow",s:"The Weasley home",
 p:[`A crooked house of several storeys near Ottery St Catchpole, in Devon, held up by magic. It has a ghoul in the attic, gnomes in the garden and a clock that shows where each member of the [[weasley|family]] is instead of the hours.`,
 `It is the first wizarding home [[harry|Harry]] knows. It served as a base for the [[ordem|Order]] in 1997 and was invaded at Bill and Fleur's wedding.`]},
alfeneiros:{t:"lugar",g:"Homes",c:"pedra",n:"4 Privet Drive",s:"The Dursleys' house",
 p:[`A suburban house in Little Whinging, Surrey, where [[harry|Harry]] was left on the night of 1 November 1981 and lived until he was seventeen, at first in the cupboard under the stairs. The [[amor|protection of Lily's blood]] lasted as long as he called that place home and was underage.`]},
godrics:{t:"lugar",g:"Homes",c:"grif",n:"Godric's Hollow",s:"Where everything began, more than once",
 p:[`A village in south-west England where wizards and Muggles have lived side by side since the Statute of Secrecy. [[godrico|Godric Gryffindor]] was born there, Ignotus [[peverell|Peverell]] and the mother and sister of [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] are buried there, and there Dumbledore met [[grindelwald|Grindelwald]].`,
 `It was where [[tiagolilian|James and Lily Potter]] hid and died in 1981. The house was left in ruins as a memorial, and there is a statue of the family in the square, which Muggles see as a war memorial.`],
 x:[["lt","Bowman Wright, inventor of the Golden Snitch, was also from Godric's Hollow."]]},
hangleton:{t:"lugar",g:"Homes",c:"trevas",n:"Little Hangleton",s:"The village of the Riddles and the Gaunts",
 p:[`An English village with the Riddle mansion on the top of the hill and the [[gaunt|Gaunts]]' hovel in the scrub. Tom Riddle killed his father and grandparents there in 1943. In the graveyard, in front of his father's grave, [[voldemort|Voldemort]] regained his body on 24 June 1995.`]},
mansaomalfoy:{t:"lugar",g:"Homes",c:"sons",n:"Malfoy Manor",s:"Voldemort's headquarters",
 p:[`The [[malfoy|Malfoys]]' stately home in Wiltshire, with white peacocks in the garden. [[voldemort|Voldemort]] made it his headquarters in 1997. In the cellar were held [[luna|Luna]], [[olivaras|Ollivander]], Dean Thomas and the goblin Griphook, and in the drawing room [[hermione|Hermione]] was tortured by [[belatriz|Bellatrix]].`]},
conchas:{t:"lugar",g:"Homes",c:"grif",n:"Shell Cottage",s:"Bill and Fleur's home",
 p:[`A seaside cottage in Cornwall, home of Bill [[weasley|Weasley]] and Fleur Delacour. It sheltered the trio and those rescued from Malfoy Manor in 1998. [[dobby|Dobby]] is buried in the garden.`]},
azkaban:{t:"lugar",g:"Prisons",c:"trevas",n:"Azkaban",s:"The wizards' prison",
 p:[`A fortress on an island in the North Sea, guarded by [[dementadores|Dementors]]. It needs no walls: the prisoners go mad or stop eating within weeks. Until 1993 no one had escaped.`,
 `[[sirius|Sirius Black]] escaped in dog form. In January 1996 ten [[comensais|Death Eaters]] broke out together, when the Dementors already obeyed [[voldemort|Voldemort]].`],
 x:[["site","The island was the fortress of Ekrizdis, a 15th-century dark wizard who lured Muggle sailors there to torture them. After his death the Ministry discovered the place, infested with Dementors."],["site","It became a prison in 1718, on the decision of Minister Damocles Rowle. A successor, Eldritch Diggory, visited the place, was horrified and died before he could change the system."]]},
nurmengard:{t:"lugar",g:"Prisons",c:"trevas",n:"Nurmengard",s:"The prison that Grindelwald built",
 p:[`A fortress raised by [[grindelwald|Grindelwald]] to imprison his enemies, with the motto 'for the greater good' carved over the entrance. After 1945 he himself was held in the highest cell, until 1998.`],
 x:[["af","The films place it in the Austrian Alps."]]},
escolas:{t:"lugar",g:"Other schools",c:"magia",n:"Beauxbatons and Durmstrang",s:"The other two great schools of Europe",
 p:[`The Beauxbatons Academy of Magic is a palace in the Pyrenees, in the south of France, headed by Madame Maxime in 1994. The Durmstrang Institute is in the far north of Europe, in a castle no outsider can locate. It has a reputation for teaching the Dark Arts and for not accepting Muggle-borns. [[grindelwald|Grindelwald]] was expelled from there.`,
 `Both came to Hogwarts for the [[tribruxo|Triwizard Tournament]]: Beauxbatons in a carriage drawn by winged horses, Durmstrang in a ship that emerged from the lake.`],
 x:[["site","Beauxbatons also takes students from Spain, Portugal, Belgium, the Netherlands and Luxembourg. [[flamel|Nicolas Flamel]] studied there."],["site","Durmstrang was founded by the Bulgarian witch Nerida Vulchanova. The grounds are extensive and lie in the mountains, with lakes."]]},
ilvermorny:{t:"lugar",g:"Other schools",c:"magia",n:"Ilvermorny",s:"The North American school",
 p:[`It stands on top of Mount Greylock, in Massachusetts, hidden from No-Majs (the American term for Muggles) by an enchanted mist.`],
 br:[["Horned Serpent","Chosen by Isolt. Represents the mind and favours scholars."],["Wampus","Chosen by Webster Boot. Represents the body and favours warriors."],["Thunderbird","Chosen by Chadwick Boot. Represents the soul and favours adventurers."],["Pukwudgie","Chosen by James Steward. Represents the heart and favours healers."]],bt:"The four houses",
 x:[["site","It was founded in 1627 by Isolt Sayre, an Irish witch descended from [[salazar|Slytherin]], who fled from her aunt, Gormlaith [[gaunt|Gaunt]], and reached America on the Mayflower. She founded the school with her No-Maj husband, James Steward, and their two adopted sons, and named it after the house where she was born."],["site","At the Sorting, the student stands on a Gordian knot carved into the floor, facing four statues. The one that wants them reacts. If more than one reacts, the student chooses."],["site","The whole story comes from the author's text published in June 2016."]]},
castelobruxo:{t:"lugar",g:"Other schools",c:"sons",n:"Castelobruxo",s:"Brazil's school of magic",
 p:[`A school hidden deep in the Amazon rainforest, taking students from all over South America. It is a square building of golden stone, like a temple, and Muggles see only a ruin there, the same trick as [[hogwarts|Hogwarts]]. The students wear bright green.`,
 `In the books it appears without a name: [[rony|Ron]] says that Bill [[weasley|Weasley]] had a pen-friend at a school in Brazil. The boy invited him on an exchange, the family could not afford it, and he, offended, sent a cursed hat that made Bill's ears shrivel.`],
 x:[["site","The name, location and description come from the author's text of January 2016. The students at Castelobruxo are especially advanced in Herbology and Magizoology, and the school offers exchanges much sought after by European students."],["site","The grounds are guarded at night by the [[caipora|Caiporas]]."],["site","Alumni mentioned: Libatius Borage, author of the Potions book Harry uses in sixth year, and João Coelho, captain of the Tarapoto Tree-Skimmers Quidditch team."]]},
outrasescolas:{t:"lugar",g:"Other schools",c:"magia",n:"Mahoutokoro, Uagadou and Koldovstoretz",s:"Japan, Africa and Russia",
 p:[`Hogwarts is one of eleven schools of magic recognised by the [[confederacao|International Confederation of Wizards]]. Eight have a known name: [[hogwarts|Hogwarts]], [[escolas|Beauxbatons, Durmstrang]], [[ilvermorny|Ilvermorny]], [[castelobruxo|Castelobruxo]] and the three below. Many countries educate their children at home or by correspondence.`],
 br:[["Mahoutokoro","Japan. The one with the fewest students, in a white jade palace at the top of an uninhabited volcanic island. The robes change colour as the student learns, from pink to gold. They turn white if the student betrays the school's code."],["Uagadou","In the Mountains of the Moon, in Uganda. The largest of all, over a thousand years old, with students from all over Africa. Students do magic with gestures, without a wand, and are strong in astronomy, alchemy and self-transfiguration."],["Koldovstoretz","Russia. Almost nothing is known beyond the name."]],bt:"The three",
 x:[["site","All of it comes from the author's texts of January 2016. Koldovstoretz was mentioned in material on the official site."]]},
/* ---------- SOCIETY ---------- */
estatuto:{t:"mundo",g:"Government and laws",c:"pedra",n:"International Statute of Wizarding Secrecy",s:"The law that hid the wizarding world",
 p:[`Signed in 1689 and in force since 1692, it obliges wizards all over the world to hide magic from Muggles. It followed centuries of persecution: burnings at the stake, young wizards attacked, families forced to use magic in the service of Muggles. A request for protection to the kings of England had been refused.`,
 `Each government is responsible for hiding the wizards, creatures and sports of its own territory. That is why Obliviators exist, why [[hogwarts|Hogwarts]] is disguised as a ruin and why it is forbidden to enchant Muggle objects. The Muggle prime minister is told of the existence of wizards on the day he takes office.`,
 `[[grindelwald|Grindelwald]] built a whole movement against the Statute.`],
 f:[["Signed","1689"],["In force","1692"]],
 x:[["lt","Clause 73, of 1750, makes each ministry responsible for hiding and controlling the magical creatures of its own territory."],["site","In the United States the separation went further. Rappaport's Law, of 1790, forbade friendship and marriage between wizards and No-Majs, and was only repealed in 1965."]]},
ministerio:{t:"mundo",g:"Government and laws",c:"pedra",n:"Ministry of Magic",s:"The wizarding government of Britain",
 p:[`It replaced the old Wizards' Council in 1707. It is headed by the Minister for Magic and operates from the [[minsede|underground headquarters in London]]. Its main job is to maintain the [[estatuto|Statute of Secrecy]].`,
 `In the story it fails almost every time: it imprisons the innocent, denies the return of [[voldemort|Voldemort]] and is finally taken over from within, on 1 August 1997, without most people noticing. It begins to register and persecute Muggle-borns.`],
 br:[["Magical Law Enforcement","The largest. Includes the Aurors and the Wizengamot, the wizards' supreme court."],["Magical Accidents and Catastrophes","The Obliviators and the Accidental Magic Reversal Squad."],["Regulation and Control of Magical Creatures","Beast, Being and Spirit Divisions."],["International Magical Cooperation","Where Barty Crouch worked."],["Magical Transportation","Floo Network, Portkeys, Apparition licences."],["Magical Games and Sports","Quidditch, the World Cup and the Triwizard Tournament."],["Mysteries","The Unspeakables."]],bt:"The seven departments",
 f:[["Ministers in the story","Cornelius Fudge (1990 to 1996), Rufus Scrimgeour (1996 to 1997), Pius Thicknesse (Voldemort's puppet) and Kingsley Shacklebolt (since 1998)"]],
 x:[["site","The author published the complete list of Ministers. The first was Ulick Gamp, in 1707. Artemisia Lufkin was the first woman, in 1798. Nobby Leach was the first Muggle-born, in 1962."],["site","Leonard Spencer-Moon governed during the war against Grindelwald and worked well with Winston Churchill."],["peca","Hermione Granger is Minister in 2020."]]},
confederacao:{t:"mundo",g:"Government and laws",c:"pedra",n:"International Confederation of Wizards",s:"The United Nations of the magical world",
 p:[`It brings together the wizarding governments and created the [[estatuto|Statute of Secrecy]]. Its head holds the title of Supreme Mugwump. [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] held the post until he was removed in 1995, for insisting that [[voldemort|Voldemort]] had returned, and regained it the following year.`,
 `The first Supreme Mugwump was Pierre Bonaccord, challenged by the wizards of Liechtenstein for wanting to ban troll-hunting.`],
 x:[["af","In the third film, the election of the early 1930s is held in Bhutan. It is won by Brazil's minister for magic, Vicência Santos, chosen by the [[qilin|Qilin]] after Dumbledore declines."]]},
macusa:{t:"mundo",g:"Government and laws",c:"pedra",n:"MACUSA",s:"The Magical Congress of the United States of America",
 p:[`The North American wizarding government does not appear in the seven books. Everything known about it comes from the author's 2016 texts and the Fantastic Beasts films.`],
 x:[["site","It was created in 1693, soon after the Statute of Secrecy and the Salem trials. Among the Salem judges were Scourers, wizard mercenaries who hunted their own kind."],["site","The United States calls Muggles No-Majs. Four wandmakers shared the market, and a licence was needed to carry a wand."],["af","In 1926 its headquarters is inside the Woolworth Building in New York, and the president is Seraphina Picquery."]]},
sangue:{t:"mundo",g:"Society",c:"pedra",n:"Blood status",s:"Pure-blood, half-blood, Muggle-born and Squib",
 p:[`The great political divide of the wizarding world. A pure-blood is someone with only wizards in the family. A half-blood has Muggles among their close ancestors. A Muggle-born is a wizard with non-magical parents, and 'Mudblood' is the insult for them. A Muggle is someone without magic. A Squib is someone born without magic into a wizarding family, like the caretaker Filch and Arabella Figg.`,
 `The idea that pure blood is worth more has no basis. Almost every family has Muggles in the tree, and those that refused to marry outside, like [[gaunt|the Gaunts]], withered. [[hermione|Hermione]] is Muggle-born. [[voldemort|Voldemort]], [[snape|Snape]] and [[harry|Harry]] are half-bloods.`,
 `It was the banner of [[salazar|Slytherin]], of the [[comensais|Death Eaters]] and of the 1997 regime, which accused Muggle-borns of having stolen magic.`],
 x:[["site","The 'Sacred Twenty-Eight' are the British families listed as pure-blood in an anonymous directory of the 1930s: Black, Malfoy, Lestrange, Gaunt, Longbottom, Weasley and Ollivander, among others. The Potters were left out."],["ent","The author compared the logic of the Death Eaters to that of the Nazi racial laws."]]},
ordem:{t:"mundo",g:"Organisations",c:"grif",n:"Order of the Phoenix",s:"The resistance to Voldemort",
 p:[`A secret society founded by [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] in the first war, outside a slow and infiltrated [[ministerio|Ministry]]. Many of the original members died, [[tiagolilian|the Potters]] among them. [[neville|Neville]]'s parents were tortured into madness.`,
 `It was reconvened on the night [[voldemort|Voldemort]] returned, in 1995, with its headquarters at [[grimmauld|Grimmauld Place]]. It brought together [[sirius|Sirius]], [[lupin|Lupin]], [[moody|Moody]], [[tonks|Tonks]], [[kingsley|Shacklebolt]], [[snape|Snape]], [[mcgonagall|McGonagall]], [[hagrid|Hagrid]] and [[weasley|the Weasleys]].`]},
comensais:{t:"mundo",g:"Organisations",c:"trevas",n:"Death Eaters",s:"Voldemort's followers",
 p:[`[[voldemort|Voldemort]]'s inner circle, marked on the left forearm with the Dark Mark, which burns when he calls. Almost all came from [[sangue|pure-blood]] families and from [[sonserina|Slytherin]], and wear hoods and masks.`,
 `Among them: [[belatriz|Bellatrix Lestrange]], Lucius [[malfoy|Malfoy]], [[pettigrew|Peter Pettigrew]], Barty [[crouch|Crouch]] Jr., Antonin Dolohov, the Carrow siblings and, until they changed sides, [[snape|Snape]] and [[regulo|Regulus Black]]. The werewolf Fenrir Greyback fought with them without having the mark.`],
 x:[["ent","The group's earlier name, in the author's drafts, was the Knights of Walpurgis."]]},
armada:{t:"mundo",g:"Organisations",c:"grif",n:"Dumbledore's Army",s:"The D.A.",
 p:[`A clandestine group of students formed in 1995, on [[hermione|Hermione]]'s idea, when [[umbridge|Umbridge]] banned the practice of defensive spells. [[harry|Harry]] gave the lessons in the [[salaprecisa|Room of Requirement]]. Members were told of meetings by enchanted fake Galleons.`,
 `Six of them fought in the [[misterios|Department of Mysteries]]. In 1997, with the trio away, [[neville|Neville]], [[gina|Ginny]] and [[luna|Luna]] re-formed the Army as resistance to the Carrows inside the castle.`]},
aurores:{t:"mundo",g:"Organisations",c:"pedra",n:"Aurors",s:"The dark wizard catchers",
 p:[`The elite force of the [[ministerio|Ministry]]. Training takes three years after Hogwarts and requires the best grades. [[moody|Moody]], [[tonks|Tonks]], [[kingsley|Shacklebolt]] and [[neville|Neville]]'s parents were Aurors.`],
 x:[["ent","Shacklebolt called into the department those who had fought in the Battle of Hogwarts, without requiring the exams. Harry, Ron and Neville served as Aurors."]]},
tribruxo:{t:"mundo",g:"Traditions",c:"magia",n:"Triwizard Tournament",s:"Three schools, three champions, three tasks",
 p:[`A competition between [[hogwarts|Hogwarts]], [[escolas|Beauxbatons and Durmstrang]], created some seven hundred years ago and suspended when deaths became too frequent. It was revived in 1994, only for students over seventeen. The Goblet of Fire chooses one champion per school, and the choice is a binding magical contract.`,
 `That year the goblet gave out four names: [[cedrico|Cedric Diggory]], Fleur Delacour, Viktor [[krum|Krum]] and [[harry|Harry]], entered by Barty [[crouch|Crouch]] Jr. The tasks were to take a golden egg from a [[dragoes|dragon]], to rescue someone from the bottom of the lake and to cross a maze. The cup at the centre was a Portkey to the graveyard where [[voldemort|Voldemort]] returned.`,
 `In the 1792 edition a cockatrice escaped and injured all three headmasters.`]},
imprensa:{t:"mundo",g:"Society",c:"pedra",n:"The wizarding press",s:"The Daily Prophet and The Quibbler",
 p:[`The Daily Prophet is the newspaper everyone reads, with moving photographs, and it tends to say what the [[ministerio|Ministry]] wants. It spent the whole of 1995 discrediting [[harry|Harry]] and [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]]. Its most famous reporter is [[skeeter|Rita Skeeter]].`,
 `The Quibbler, edited by Xenophilius Lovegood, publishes wild theories about creatures that do not exist. It was also the only paper to publish Harry's account of the return of [[voldemort|Voldemort]] and, in 1997, to support the resistance.`]},
ordemmerlin:{t:"mundo",g:"Traditions",c:"magia",n:"Order of Merlin and Chocolate Frogs",s:"How wizards remember their heroes",
 p:[`The Order of Merlin is the greatest decoration in the wizarding world, in three classes. [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] held First Class for his victory over [[grindelwald|Grindelwald]]. [[fudge|Fudge]] gave himself First Class.`,
 `Its popular fame comes from the cards of famous wizards that come with Chocolate Frogs. It was on one of them that [[harry|Harry]] first read the name of [[flamel|Nicolas Flamel]].`],
 x:[["ent","Harry, Ron and Hermione got their own cards after the war. Ron considers this the best moment of his life."]]},
quadribol:{t:"mundo",g:"Traditions",c:"magia",n:"Quidditch",s:"The wizards' sport",
 p:[`Played on broomsticks, by two teams of seven, with four balls. It began in the 11th century on Queerditch Marsh and became the most popular sport in the wizarding world. At Hogwarts the four houses compete for the Quidditch Cup every year.`,
 `[[harry|Harry]] joined the [[grifinoria|Gryffindor]] team at eleven, as Seeker. The rules, history, teams and World Cup are in the Quidditch section of this page.`]},
});
/* ---------- TIMELINE ---------- */
// ev: [year, title, text, highlight?]
const ERAS = [
{id:"origens",n:"Origins",r:"to 1689",c:"magia",h:"From the founders to the time of the burnings",
 intro:`The seven books give almost no ancient dates. What is known about this period comes from History of Magic lessons, the Hogwarts textbooks and the texts the author published later.`,
 ev:[["382 BC","The Ollivanders open their workshop",`The [[olivaras|Ollivander]] family begins making [[varinhas|wands]]. It is the date on the sign of the Diagon Alley shop.`],
 ["Antiquity","Herpo the Foul",`In ancient Greece, a dark wizard creates the first [[basilisco|basilisk]] and the first known [[horcruxes|Horcrux]].`],
 ["c. 990","The founding of Hogwarts",`[[godrico|Gryffindor]], [[helga|Hufflepuff]], [[rowena|Ravenclaw]] and [[salazar|Slytherin]] raise [[hogwarts|Hogwarts]] away from the eyes of Muggles, in a time of persecution. Each chooses students by what they value most, and so the four houses are born.`,1],
 ["Years later","Slytherin leaves the school",`Slytherin wants to bar the children of Muggles, loses the argument with Gryffindor and leaves, having left behind the [[camara|Chamber of Secrets]]. The founders enchant the [[chapeu|Sorting Hat]] so that the Sorting can go on without them.`],
 ["c. 1050","The game on Queerditch Marsh",`The diary of the witch Gertie Keddle records neighbours playing ball on broomsticks. It is the first account of what would become [[quadribol|Quidditch]].`],
 ["1269","The Snidget hunt",`Barberus Bragge, head of the Wizards' Council, lets a [[pomorim|Golden Snidget]] loose in a game and offers 150 Galleons to whoever catches it. The position of Seeker is born.`],
 ["13th century","The Peverell brothers",`Antioch, Cadmus and Ignotus [[peverell|Peverell]] live in Godric's Hollow. Legend says they received the three [[reliquias|Hallows]] from Death.`],
 ["13th century","The first Triwizard Tournament",`Hogwarts, Beauxbatons and Durmstrang create the [[tribruxo|Triwizard Tournament]], held every five years.`],
 ["1473","The first Quidditch World Cup",`The final, between Transylvania and Flanders, becomes famous for having seen all seven hundred possible fouls.`],
 ["1492","The death of Nearly Headless Nick",`Sir Nicholas de Mimsy-Porpington is executed on 31 October with a blunt axe and returns as the ghost of [[grifinoria|Gryffindor]].`],
 ["15th century","Ekrizdis and the island of Azkaban",`A dark wizard raises a fortress in the North Sea. After his death, the place is found overrun with [[dementadores|Dementors]]: it is the future [[azkaban|Azkaban]].`],
 ["1612","The goblin rebellion",`One of the many [[duendes|goblin]] revolts against wizards takes place on the outskirts of [[hogsmeade|Hogsmeade]].`],
 ["1627","The founding of Ilvermorny",`Isolt Sayre, a descendant of Slytherin, founds the school of [[ilvermorny|Ilvermorny]] in the United States.`],
 ["1674","The Quidditch League",`The thirteen best teams form the Quidditch League of Great Britain and Ireland. The rest are disbanded.`]]},
{id:"sigilo",n:"Secrecy",r:"1689 to 1880",c:"pedra",h:"The wizarding world goes into hiding",
 intro:`With the Statute of Secrecy, wizards leave Muggle history and come to have governments, laws and institutions of their own. Almost everything Harry finds in 1991 was put together in these two centuries.`,
 ev:[["1689","The International Statute of Wizarding Secrecy",`The [[confederacao|International Confederation of Wizards]] signs the [[estatuto|Statute]], which takes effect in 1692. Wizarding families move to villages such as [[godrics|Godric's Hollow]], where they can protect one another.`,1],
 ["1693","MACUSA",`The wizards of North America create the [[macusa|Magical Congress]], a year after the Salem trials.`],
 ["1707","The Ministry of Magic",`The Wizards' Council gives way to the [[ministerio|Ministry of Magic]]. The first Minister is Ulick Gamp.`,1],
 ["1709","Breeding dragons becomes a crime",`The Warlocks' Convention bans the breeding of [[dragoes|dragons]].`],
 ["1717","The Unforgivable Curses",`Imperius, Cruciatus and the Killing Curse are classed as [[imperdoaveis|Unforgivable]].`],
 ["1718","Azkaban becomes a prison",`Minister Damocles Rowle begins sending convicts to [[azkaban|Azkaban]], in the care of the Dementors.`],
 ["1750","Rules for beasts and for Quidditch",`Clause 73 of the Statute obliges each government to hide the [[classificacao|magical creatures]] of its territory. In the same year the Department of Magical Games and Sports fixes the rules of [[quadribol|Quidditch]].`],
 ["1790","Rappaport's Law",`After a serious breach of secrecy, MACUSA bans any contact between wizards and No-Majs in the United States.`],
 ["1792","The Triwizard is suspended",`A cockatrice injures the three headmasters, and the [[tribruxo|tournament]] is not held for two centuries.`],
 ["1811","What is a being",`Minister Grogan Stump defines [[classificacao|Beings, Beasts and Spirits]] and ends a debate of five hundred years.`],
 ["1827 to 1835","The Hogwarts Express",`Minister Ottaline Gambol solves the problem of getting hundreds of students to Scotland without attracting attention: a train. See [[transporte|magical transport]].`],
 ["1875","Underage magic",`A decree forbids underage wizards from doing magic outside school. See [[rastreador|the Trace]].`]]},
{id:"grindelwald",n:"Grindelwald",r:"1881 to 1945",c:"trevas",h:"Dumbledore, Grindelwald and the wizards' world war",
 intro:`The books tell this period in a few pages, almost all of them in Deathly Hallows. The Fantastic Beasts films fill the whole of it, and whatever comes only from them is marked.`,
 ev:[["1881","Albus Dumbledore is born",`[[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] is born in Mould-on-the-Wold. Years later his father is imprisoned for attacking the Muggle boys who hurt [[aberforth|Ariana]], and the family moves to [[godrics|Godric's Hollow]].`],
 ["1897","Newt Scamander is born",`The future author of Fantastic Beasts and Where to Find Them. See [[newt|Newt Scamander]].`],
 ["1899","The summer in Godric's Hollow",`Dumbledore finishes school, loses his mother and meets [[grindelwald|Grindelwald]]. The two plan the search for the [[reliquias|Hallows]] and wizard dominion. The duel with Aberforth kills Ariana, and Grindelwald flees.`,1],
 ["1926","Tom Riddle is born. New York is shaken",`On 31 December, Merope [[gaunt|Gaunt]] gives birth to [[voldemort|Tom Marvolo Riddle]] in a London orphanage and dies. In the films, in the same month, [[newt|Newt]] arrives in New York, [[credence|Credence]]'s [[obscurus|Obscurus]] destroys part of the city, and Grindelwald is arrested by [[macusa|MACUSA]].`,1],
 ["1927","Newt's book. Paris",`Fantastic Beasts and Where to Find Them is published. In the films, Grindelwald escapes and gathers followers at a rally in the Père-Lachaise cemetery, in Paris.`],
 ["1930s","The election in Bhutan",`Only in the films: Grindelwald tries to rig the choice of head of the [[confederacao|International Confederation]] with a dead [[qilin|Qilin]]. The blood pact with Dumbledore is broken. The one elected is the Brazilian Vicência Santos.`],
 ["1938","Dumbledore seeks out Tom Riddle",`The Transfiguration professor visits the orphanage and tells the eleven-year-old boy that he is a wizard. Riddle already knows how to hurt others with his mind and speaks to snakes.`],
 ["1943","The Chamber of Secrets is opened",`Riddle, in fifth year, looses the [[basilisco|basilisk]]. Myrtle dies in the bathroom in June, and he frames [[hagrid|Hagrid]]. In the summer he kills his father and grandparents in [[hangleton|Little Hangleton]] and makes his first [[horcruxes|Horcruxes]].`,1],
 ["1945","The duel",`Dumbledore faces Grindelwald and wins. He takes the Elder Wand, and Grindelwald goes to [[nurmengard|Nurmengard]]. In the same year Riddle graduates from Hogwarts.`,1]]},
{id:"guerra1",n:"First War",r:"1945 to 1981",c:"sons",h:"The rise of Voldemort",
 intro:`The first wizarding war lasts about eleven years and is told in memories: in the Pensieve, in the stories of Sirius, Lupin and Hagrid. The dates come from the characters' ages and from gravestones.`,
 ev:[["1940s","The cup and the locket",`An employee of Borgin and Burkes, Riddle kills the collector Hepzibah Smith and steals Hufflepuff's cup and Slytherin's locket. He vanishes for ten years and returns as [[voldemort|Lord Voldemort]].`],
 ["1950s","The refused job",`Voldemort asks [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]], by now headmaster, for the post of Defence Against the [[trevas|Dark Arts]]. He is refused, curses the post and uses the visit to hide the diadem in the [[salaprecisa|Room of Requirement]].`],
 ["1970","The war begins",`Voldemort and the [[comensais|Death Eaters]] go over to open terror: disappearances, murders, giants and [[inferi|Inferi]]. Dumbledore founds the [[ordem|Order of the Phoenix]].`,1],
 ["1971","The Marauders arrive at Hogwarts",`[[tiagolilian|James Potter]], [[sirius|Sirius Black]], [[lupin|Remus Lupin]], [[pettigrew|Peter Pettigrew]], Lily Evans and [[snape|Severus Snape]] begin first year. The Whomping Willow is planted for Lupin.`],
 ["1979","The death of Regulus Black",`[[regulo|Regulus]] swaps the locket in the cave for a fake and dies in the lake.`],
 ["1980","The prophecy",`At the Hog's Head, [[trelawney|Sybill Trelawney]] makes the [[profecia|prophecy]] before Dumbledore. Snape hears half and tells Voldemort. [[neville|Neville]] is born on 30 July, and [[harry|Harry]] on the 31st.`,1],
 ["31 Oct 1981","Godric's Hollow",`Betrayed by Pettigrew, James and Lily are killed. The Killing Curse cast at Harry rebounds on Voldemort, who loses his body. [[hagrid|Hagrid]] takes the baby to [[alfeneiros|Privet Drive]].`,1],
 ["Nov 1981","The arrests",`Sirius corners Pettigrew, who fakes his own death and kills twelve Muggles. Sirius goes to [[azkaban|Azkaban]] without trial. [[belatriz|Bellatrix Lestrange]] and [[crouch|Barty Crouch Jr.]] torture the Longbottoms and are convicted.`]]},
{id:"harry",n:"Harry's Years",r:"1991 to 1998",c:"grif",h:"The seven books",
 intro:`Each book covers a school year, from September to June, beginning with the preceding summer. The last is the only one set outside school.`,
 ev:[["1991 to 1992","The Philosopher's Stone",`Harry discovers he is a wizard, enters [[grifinoria|Gryffindor]] and meets [[rony|Ron]] and [[hermione|Hermione]]. Voldemort, clinging to the back of Professor Quirrell's head, tries to steal the [[pedrafilosofal|Philosopher's Stone]] and is stopped in front of the [[ojesed|Mirror of Erised]].`,1],
 ["1992 to 1993","The Chamber of Secrets",`Riddle's diary possesses [[gina|Ginny Weasley]] and reopens the [[camara|Chamber of Secrets]]. Harry kills the [[basilisco|basilisk]] with the [[espada|Sword of Gryffindor]] and destroys the diary, not knowing it was a [[horcruxes|Horcrux]]. [[dobby|Dobby]] is freed.`,1],
 ["1993 to 1994","The Prisoner of Azkaban",`[[sirius|Sirius Black]] escapes. [[dementadores|Dementors]] surround the school, and [[lupin|Lupin]] teaches Harry the [[patrono|Patronus]]. In the [[gritos|Shrieking Shack]] the truth comes out: the traitor was [[pettigrew|Pettigrew]], who escapes. A [[viratempo|Time-Turner]] saves Sirius and Buckbeak.`,1],
 ["1994","The Quidditch World Cup",`Ireland beats Bulgaria 170 to 160. After the match, masked [[comensais|Death Eaters]] attack the campsite, and the Dark Mark appears in the sky for the first time in thirteen years.`],
 ["1994 to 1995","The Goblet of Fire",`Hogwarts hosts the [[tribruxo|Triwizard Tournament]]. On 24 June the cup takes Harry and [[cedrico|Cedric]] to the graveyard at [[hangleton|Little Hangleton]]. Cedric is killed, and [[voldemort|Voldemort]] regains his body with Harry's blood. Minister [[fudge|Fudge]] refuses to believe it.`,1],
 ["1995 to 1996","The Order of the Phoenix",`The [[ordem|Order]] is reconvened. [[umbridge|Umbridge]] takes over Hogwarts, and the students create [[armada|Dumbledore's Army]]. In June, in the [[misterios|Department of Mysteries]], Sirius dies and the Ministry sees Voldemort. Harry hears the whole [[profecia|prophecy]].`,1],
 ["1996 to 1997","The Half-Blood Prince",`Dumbledore shows Harry Riddle's past and the secret of the [[horcruxes|Horcruxes]]. Draco [[malfoy|Malfoy]] opens the castle to the Death Eaters. On 30 June [[snape|Snape]] kills [[dumbledore|Dumbledore]] on the Astronomy Tower.`,1],
 ["27 Jul 1997","The Seven Potters",`The Order takes Harry out of his aunt and uncle's house with six decoys. [[moody|Moody]] and the owl Hedwig die, and George Weasley loses an ear.`],
 ["1 Aug 1997","The fall of the Ministry",`Minister Scrimgeour is killed. The [[ministerio|Ministry]] passes into Voldemort's hands, who rules through Pius Thicknesse. Harry, Ron and Hermione flee the wedding at [[toca|The Burrow]] and begin the Horcrux hunt.`,1],
 ["1997 to 1998","The Deathly Hallows",`The trio break into the Ministry and recover the locket. Ron leaves and returns. In Godric's Hollow, Harry nearly dies. Xenophilius Lovegood tells the story of the [[reliquias|Hallows]]. Captured, they are taken to [[mansaomalfoy|Malfoy Manor]], and [[dobby|Dobby]] dies saving them. They break into [[gringotes|Gringotts]] and escape on a dragon.`,1],
 ["2 May 1998","The Battle of Hogwarts",`In a single night the diadem, the cup and Nagini fall. Fred [[weasley|Weasley]], Lupin, [[tonks|Tonks]], Snape and dozens of others die. Harry discovers he is a Horcrux, gives himself up in the [[floresta|Forbidden Forest]] and returns. In the Great Hall, at dawn, Voldemort's curse rebounds on him.`,1]]},
{id:"depois",n:"Afterwards",r:"1998 to 2020",c:"lufa",h:"Nineteen years later, and beyond",
 intro:`The epilogue of the seventh book is only a few pages long. Almost everything known about the post-war years comes from the author's interviews in 2007, the texts on the official site and the 2016 play.`,
 ev:[["1998","The reform",`[[kingsley|Kingsley Shacklebolt]] is confirmed as Minister. According to the author, he removes the [[dementadores|Dementors]] from [[azkaban|Azkaban]] and brings Harry, Ron and Neville into the [[aurores|Aurors]]. [[mcgonagall|McGonagall]] takes over Hogwarts. [[hermione|Hermione]] goes back to finish her studies.`,1],
 ["2007","Harry heads the Aurors",`In interviews, the author says that [[harry|Harry]] takes over the department at 26 and that [[hermione|Hermione]] works to overturn the laws favouring [[sangue|pure-bloods]].`],
 ["2014","The World Cup in Patagonia",`In the official site's texts, signed by [[gina|Ginny]] and [[skeeter|Rita Skeeter]], [[krum|Krum]]'s Bulgaria beats Brazil in the [[quadribol|Quidditch]] World Cup final. [[armada|Dumbledore's Army]] meets again in the stands.`],
 ["1 Sep 2017","Nineteen years later",`The epilogue. At platform 9¾, Harry and Ginny see off James and Albus Severus. Ron and Hermione see off Rose. Draco [[malfoy|Malfoy]] sees off Scorpius. Teddy Lupin is almost grown, and [[neville|Neville]] is a professor. The scar has not hurt for nineteen years.`,1],
 ["2017 to 2020","The Cursed Child",`The play begins in the same scene. [[delphi|Albus and Scorpius]] go to [[sonserina|Slytherin]], steal a [[viratempo|Time-Turner]] and nearly undo the victory of 1998. Hermione is Minister for Magic.`]]}
];

/* ---------- QUIDDITCH ---------- */
// Pitch items. n: name. l: label drawn on the pitch. k: letter on the player marker (when there is one). q: how many per team. c: color key. p: text.
const QITEMS = {
goleiro:{n:"Keeper",l:"Keeper",k:"K",q:"1 per team",c:"corv",p:`Stands in front of the three hoops and stops goals. It is the oldest position in the game. At first the Keeper also attacked. In time the Keeper came to stay in the scoring area. For Harry's Gryffindor, the Keepers were Oliver Wood and, later, Ron.`},
artilheiro:{n:"Chasers",l:"Chasers",k:"C",q:"3 per team",c:"grif",p:`They pass the Quaffle among themselves and try to throw it through one of the opposing hoops. Each goal is worth 10 points. Only one Chaser at a time may enter the scoring area. James Potter and Ginny Weasley played in this position.`},
batedor:{n:"Beaters",l:"Beaters",k:"B",q:"2 per team",c:"sons",p:`They carry short bats and spend the game knocking the Bludgers away from their teammates and towards the opponents. They do not touch the Quaffle or the Snitch. Fred and George Weasley were Gryffindor's pair.`},
apanhador:{n:"Seeker",l:"Seeker",k:"S",q:"1 per team",c:"lufa",p:`Has only one task: find and catch the Golden Snitch. The catch is worth 150 points and ends the match. Usually the lightest and fastest player, and the one who suffers most fouls. Harry, Draco Malfoy, Cedric Diggory and Cho Chang were Seekers for their houses. Viktor Krum is Bulgaria's.`},
goles:{n:"Quaffle",l:"Quaffle",q:"1 in play",c:"grif",p:`The scoring ball. It is red leather, about 12 inches (30 cm) across, with no visible seam, and enchanted to fall slowly when someone drops it. It has been red since 1711, so that it does not vanish in the mud.`},
balaco:{n:"Bludgers",l:"Bludgers",q:"2 in play",c:"sons",p:`Two iron balls of about 10 inches (25 cm), enchanted to chase the nearest player, from any team, and knock them off their broom. They began as enchanted rocks. In 1992 Dobby tampered with one so that it hunted only Harry.`},
pomo:{n:"Golden Snitch",l:"Golden Snitch",q:"1 in play",c:"lufa",p:`A small golden ball the size of a walnut, with silver wings, fast and almost invisible. It was invented by Bowman Wright, of Godric's Hollow, to replace the Golden Snidget, the bird hunted in games since 1269. It has a flesh memory: it recognises the first person who touched it. Dumbledore hid the Resurrection Stone inside the first Snitch Harry caught.`},
aros:{n:"Hoops and pitch",l:"Hoops",q:"3 hoops per side",c:"corv",p:`The pitch is an oval 500 feet long by 180 wide, about 152 by 55 metres, with a small central circle from which the balls are released. At each end stand three golden poles 50 feet tall, about 15 metres, each topped with a hoop. Until 1883 the goals were baskets. The switch to hoops of standard size caused riots.`}
};
const QTABS = [
["regras","Rules",`<div class="prose"><p>Two teams of seven players: three Chasers, two Beaters, a Keeper and a Seeker. A goal with the Quaffle is worth 10 points. Catching the Golden Snitch is worth 150 and ends the game. Whoever has the most points wins, so it is possible to catch the Snitch and lose, as Bulgaria did in the 1994 final.</p><p>There is no time limit. The match ends only with the capture of the Snitch or by agreement of the two captains. Oliver Wood tells Harry that the record is three months. There is no substitution, even in case of injury. Players may carry a wand, but may not use it against anyone.</p><p>The Department of Magical Games and Sports lists seven hundred fouls, and the complete list has never been released, so as not to give anyone ideas. Ten are common.</p></div><ul class="branches"><li><b>Blagging.</b> Seizing the tail of an opponent's broom.</li><li><b>Blatching.</b> Flying with intent to collide.</li><li><b>Blurting.</b> Locking broom handles to send the other player off course.</li><li><b>Bumphing.</b> Hitting a Bludger towards the crowd.</li><li><b>Cobbing.</b> Excessive use of elbows.</li><li><b>Flacking.</b> The Keeper passing their body through the hoop to defend.</li><li><b>Haversacking.</b> Having a hand on the Quaffle when it passes through the hoop.</li><li><b>Quaffle-pocking.</b> Tampering with the Quaffle.</li><li><b>Snitchnip.</b> Any player other than the Seeker touching the Snitch.</li><li><b>Stooging.</b> More than one Chaser inside the scoring area.</li></ul><div class="prose"><p>Famous plays include the Wronski Feint, in which the Seeker dives, pretending to have seen the Snitch, to make the rival crash into the ground, and the Hawkshead Attacking Formation, for Chasers.</p></div>`],
["historia","History",`<dl class="war"><dt>c. 1050</dt><dd>The witch Gertie Keddle notes in her diary a ball game on brooms on Queerditch Marsh. There is already a leather ball and enchanted rocks that attack the players.</dd><dt>c. 1150</dt><dd>A letter from the wizard Goodwin Kneen describes 'Kwidditch' with organised teams, goals as barrels on stakes and the 'blooders', the future Bludgers.</dd><dt>1269</dt><dd>Barberus Bragge lets a Golden Snidget loose in a game in Kent and offers 150 Galleons for its capture. The witch Modesty Rabnott saves the bird and is fined. Snidget hunting becomes part of the game.</dd><dt>14th century</dt><dd>The Snidget becomes a protected species. Bowman Wright invents the Golden Snitch.</dd><dt>1362 and 1368</dt><dd>Playing within 50 miles, and later within 100 miles, of any Muggle town is forbidden.</dd><dt>1473</dt><dd>First World Cup.</dd><dt>1620</dt><dd>Quintius Umfraville publishes The Noble Sport of Warlocks, with the pitch already divided into scoring areas.</dd><dt>1674</dt><dd>Creation of the League of Great Britain and Ireland.</dd><dt>1711</dt><dd>The Quaffle becomes red.</dd><dt>1750</dt><dd>The Department of Magical Games and Sports fixes the official rules.</dd><dt>1875</dt><dd>Daisy Pennifold creates the slow-falling Quaffle. In the same year comes the spell that lets it be held in one hand.</dd><dt>1883</dt><dd>Baskets give way to hoops.</dd></dl>`],
["times","Teams",`<div class="prose"><p>Since 1674 the League of Great Britain and Ireland has had thirteen teams. All the others were invited to disband.</p></div><div class="scroll"><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Team</th><th>From</th><th>Since</th><th>Colours and reputation</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Appleby Arrows</td><td>Northern England</td><td>1612</td><td>Light blue with a silver arrow.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Ballycastle Bats</td><td>Northern Ireland</td><td>—</td><td>Black with a scarlet bat. 27 titles.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Caerphilly Catapults</td><td>Wales</td><td>1402</td><td>Pale green and scarlet stripes. 18 titles.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Chudley Cannons</td><td>England</td><td>—</td><td>Bright orange. 21 titles, the last in 1892. Ron's team.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Falmouth Falcons</td><td>Cornwall</td><td>—</td><td>Dark grey and white. Famous for rough play.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Holyhead Harpies</td><td>Wales</td><td>1203</td><td>Dark green with a golden claw. Witches only. Ginny Weasley played for them.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Kenmare Kestrels</td><td>Ireland</td><td>1291</td><td>Emerald green with two yellow Ks.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Montrose Magpies</td><td>Scotland</td><td>—</td><td>Black and white. 32 titles, the biggest champion.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Pride of Portree</td><td>Isle of Skye, Scotland</td><td>1292</td><td>Purple with a gold star.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Puddlemere United</td><td>England</td><td>1163</td><td>Navy blue with two golden bulrushes. The oldest. Oliver Wood joined as a reserve.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Tutshill Tornados</td><td>England</td><td>1520</td><td>Sky blue. Five titles in a row in the early 20th century.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wigtown Wanderers</td><td>Scotland</td><td>1422</td><td>Blood red with a silver cleaver.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wimbourne Wasps</td><td>England</td><td>1312</td><td>Yellow and black stripes. Ludo Bagman was a Beater.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>`],
["copa","World Cup",`<div class="prose"><p>Held every four years since 1473. It is the biggest event in the wizarding world and the biggest challenge to the Statute of Secrecy: a hundred thousand wizards camped in one place.</p></div><dl class="war"><dt>1473</dt><dd>Transylvania against Flanders. All seven hundred fouls were committed, among them turning a Chaser into a weasel and trying to behead the Keeper with a sword.</dd><dt>1877</dt><dd>The tournament no one remembers. According to the author's text, the Cup took place, tickets and programmes were left over, and no living wizard recalls a single match.</dd><dt>1994</dt><dd>In England. Ireland 170, Bulgaria 160. Viktor Krum caught the Snitch with his team behind by 160, to end the game on his own terms. The mascots were leprechauns and Veela.</dd><dt>2014</dt><dd>In the Patagonian desert, in Argentina. Brazil knocked out Wales in the quarter-finals and the United States in the semi-final, with Seeker Tony Silva, and lost the final to Krum's Bulgaria, who came back from retirement at 38. The coverage was published on the official site in July 2014, by Ginny Potter.</dd></dl>`],
["vassouras","Brooms",`<div class="prose"><p>European wizards have flown on brooms since at least the 10th century. The first ones were uncomfortable and slow. The racing broom was only born with the Cushioning Charm of 1820 and the factories of the 20th century.</p></div><dl class="war"><dt>1879</dt><dd>Oakshaft 79. Sturdy, made for long distances. It was the first to cross the Atlantic.</dd><dt>1901</dt><dd>Moontrimmer. It reached unprecedented heights.</dd><dt>1926</dt><dd>Cleansweep One, by the Ollerton brothers. The first mass-produced for sport.</dd><dt>1929</dt><dd>Comet 140, by Keitch and Horton, with the first braking charm.</dd><dt>1967</dt><dd>Nimbus 1000. It reached 100 mph and could spin on its own axis.</dd><dt>1991</dt><dd>Nimbus 2000. Harry's first broom, a gift from Professor McGonagall.</dd><dt>1992</dt><dd>Nimbus 2001. Lucius Malfoy bought one for every Slytherin player.</dd><dt>1993</dt><dd>Firebolt. From zero to 150 mph in ten seconds. A gift from Sirius to Harry.</dd></dl>`],
["outros","Other games",`<ul class="branches"><li><b>Quodpot.</b> The American game, with eleven per team. The ball, the quod, explodes, and you must put it in the cauldron before it does. It began in the 18th century from a defective Quaffle in an English wizard's luggage.</li><li><b>The Swedish annual broom race.</b> It has existed since the 10th century. It covers more than 300 miles (480 km), with the course crossing a dragon reserve.</li><li><b>Creaothceann.</b> A Scottish game in which each player tied a cauldron to their head to catch enchanted rocks falling from the sky. Banned in 1762.</li><li><b>Aingingein.</b> Irish: crossing a row of burning barrels with a ball made from a goat's bladder.</li><li><b>Shuntbumps and Swivenhodge.</b> English games of knocking the opponent off the broom and of batting a pig's bladder over a hedge.</li><li><b>Wizard's chess, Gobstones and Exploding Snap.</b> The parlour games of Hogwarts students. In chess the pieces move by themselves and really destroy one another.</li></ul>`]
];

